+From 4b2f61310d308c0444f211449b330351a777aea5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Talaria <324092415+talaria0101@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 12:07:52 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH 2/2] add validation suite, experiments, reviews, and reference
+ corpus
+
+* tests-ext/: the self-contained validator (validate.sh), hostile test
+  targets (anti-debug detector that exits 42 when traced; display-less
+  early-exiter with a hidden dlopen fallback; static variant), and the
+  ptrace-free unit tests (JSON escaper, report collector) that run even
+  inside ptrace-restricted sandboxes.
+* experiments/: numbered, re-runnable scripts with committed logs; the
+  negative result that shaped the layout (the development host denies
+  ptrace via seccomp -- evidence in logs/10-ptrace-map.txt) is kept.
+* docs/reviews/: the three documented review passes (code, behaviour,
+  claims/reproducibility) with findings and resolutions.
+* references/: strace tracker corpus (fetched read-only via the public
+  proxy with scripts from the operator's methodology; see
+  references/strace__strace/PROVENANCE.md), quick-sharun.sh, and the
+  Anylinux-AppImages README that document the status-quo pain points.
+* README.md: repository front page; the upstream strace README is
+  preserved verbatim as README-strace.md.
