++  "updated_at": "2017-11-03T03:23:04Z",
++  "body": "Well, you can't prohibit strace's testsuite to call whatever syscalls it wants. And it does so for a good measure\u2014to check whether they are decoded correctly. Of course, it would be better to have some shim instead of real kernel for testing these boundary cases that involve undefined behaviour, but, unfortunately, we're not there yet.\r\n\r\nSo far, I'd like to propose another approach\u2014let's allow the possibility of having EINVAL as one of possible outcomes of the call. For example: https://github.com/esyr/strace/commit/407c2676aff32677dfe766e17bd6468521b19375 . I haven't tested this one yet, however.",
