++  "updated_at": "2017-11-12T16:13:45Z",
++  "body": "I don't see a generic way to implement the \"any process which is PTRACE_ATTACH-ed or PTRACE_SEIZE-d\" part: we can try to do it for the cases where both the initiator and target are traced by the same strace process, but this is too custom functionality, from my point of view. I'd suggest to augment Lua interface with a possibility to search for specific tracee and detach/drop it. Another concern is that since arbitrary pIds in arguments shoud be processed, it should be done in a PID NS-aware way, and strace is not PID NS-aware, currently.\r\n\r\nBut at least PTRACE_TRACEME part can be relatively easy implemented.",
