++  "body": "This is due to get_sockaddr_by_inode sometimes fails to find the respective socket for the given inode (it iterates through all of them via sock_diag and can't find the requested one), so the socket family can't be determined and, as a result, proper xlat for decoding netlink message type can't be selected.\r\n\r\nIt looks like a race within kernel, but I'm not entirely sure yet about it.",
