++  "updated_at": "2018-01-23T16:04:47Z",
++  "body": "The thing you should understand is that the \"medicinal effects\" are _caused_ by the overhead.  Running the program under strace makes it go slower and more serially, and that makes it harder to hit timing-sensitive bugs.  Reducing the amount of overhead might very well make the problem come back.\r\n\r\nThe thing to _try_ is running the program under `valgrind` instead, in both the default and \"helgrind\" modes; that will be even slower but has a fighting chance of finding the actual bug so it can be fixed properly.",
