++  "body": "Yes, it does formally look like a success, I agree.\r\n\r\nBut as for the stated purpose of the feature (\"An option to be able to check why a program which do not print any error message fail.\"), it is another example of an effect of a syscall which means that something failed.\r\n\r\nI don't insist on including this case into the suggested option/filter; this might be not formally correct. But it seems like a related wish; useful if looking for output which gives hints why a program failed.\r\n\r\n          POLLERR\r\n               Error condition (only returned in revents; ignored\r\n               in events).\r\n\r\n          POLLNVAL\r\n               Invalid  request: fd  not open  (only returned  in\r\n               revents; ignored in events).\r\n\r\nCompare to a similar failure of `connect`:\r\n\r\n     EBADF\r\n          sockfd is not a valid open file descriptor.\r\n",
