++  "body": "I make  tests with libtool and without libtool and find that the error has nothing to do with libtool.But I find other thing below.\r\nI review the code once again in both Ubuntu 16.04 and Ubuntu 14.04, and find if I executive 'autoconf' at the first time,there are some error below:\r\n\r\n> configure.ac:45: error: possibly undefined macro: AM_INIT_AUTOMAKE\r\n>       If this token and others are legitimate, please use m4_pattern_allow.\r\n>       See the Autoconf documentation.\r\n> configure.ac:46: error: possibly undefined macro: AM_MAINTAINER_MODE\r\n> configure.ac:921: error: possibly undefined macro: AM_CONDITIONAL\r\n\r\nand 'autoconf' once again,there is no error.\r\nSo the fact is that the error only occurs at the first time and report 3 possibly undefined macro.",
