++  "body": "Interestingly, the commit message for clang claims it is in `-Wextra` too...\r\n```\r\ncommit 57dc2fc543e4cd3def9d27f22349f5b3c6513f4c\r\nAuthor: Douglas Gregor <dgregor@apple.com>\r\nDate:   Mon Jun 14 21:15:09 2010 +0000\r\n\r\n    Put warnings about designated initializations overridding prior\r\n    initializations into their own warning group, initializer-overrides,\r\n    which is part of -Wextra. Patch by william@25thandClement.com, fixes\r\n    PR6934!\r\n```\r\nAnyway, the warning exists since clang 2.8 (which is so absurdly old no one will use it), and `_Pragma` exists more or less since its inception, as far as I can tell.",
