++  "body": "`++ sed -r -n 's/#define[[:space:]]*COPYRIGHT_YEAR[[:space:]]*\"([^\"]*)\".*/\\1/p' ../../config.h`\r\n`+ config_year=`\r\n`+ '[' 2019 -ge '' ']'`\r\n`./strace-V.test: line 36: [: : integer expression expected`\r\n`+ echo 'The year derived from config.h () does not pass sanity checks.'`\r\nMay I ask you to provide `config.h` from the build tree?\r\n\r\n`BPF_MAP_CREATE failed: Operation not permitted`\r\nThis one can occur when locked memory limit (`ulimit -l`) is too tight and/or number of make jobs is too high (each map requires one page of locked memory, at least, and it is (counter-intuitively) accounted for all user's tasks and not for each task separately).\r\n\r\n`BPF_PROG_LOAD failed (log: \"\"): Bad address`\r\nThis one is strange. On what kernel are you running the test suite?",
