++  "body": "There is a delay indeed when the locked memory is being reclaimed after a BPF program or map is removed. If I understand correctly it could come from the `call_rcu()` in [`__bpf_put_prog_noref()`](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/kernel/bpf/syscall.c?h=v5.4#n1339).\r\n\r\nFor the record, in bpftool we call `setrlimit()` to work around it and [raise the limit](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=8302b9bd31d29f29dd24dd6b1e1e5682c302c11c) prior to running a succession of tests to check what BPF objects are supported by the system.",
