++  "body": "Sorry, it seems I had a misunderstanding (for dozen of years?) on how exactly verbose flags `-v` and `-e verbose=...` interact between themselves. They were cleared after studying codebase more thoroughly.\r\nThis actually works as I have generally desired:\r\n```bash\r\nstrace --seccomp-bpf -qftttzs4096 -Xraw -e verbose=execve,execveat -e trace=%process -e signal=none -o/dev/stdout -- sh -c '/bin/true {0001..0100} & wait'\r\n```\r\nAnd it produces output with all required `timestamp, ARGV, ppid` without ENVP:\r\n```strace\r\n163855 1582630469.899427 execve(\"/usr/bin/sh\", [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"/bin/true {0001..0100} & wait\"], 0x7ffe0343f838 /* 45 vars */) = 0\r\n163855 1582630469.900059 arch_prctl(0x1002, 0x7fda8c953b80) = 0\r\n163855 1582630469.903170 clone(child_stack=NULL, flags=0x1200000|17, child_tidptr=0x7fda8c953e50) = 163856\r\n163856 1582630469.903816 execve(\"/bin/true\", [\"/bin/true\", \"0001\", \"0002\", \"0003\", \"0004\", \"0005\", \"0006\", \"0007\", \"0008\", \"0009\", \"0010\", \"0011\", \"0012\", \"0013\", \"0014\", \"0015\", \"0016\", \"0017\", \"0018\", \"0019\", \"0020\", \"0021\", \"0022\", \"0023\", \"0024\", \"0025\", \"0026\", \"0027\", \"0028\", \"0029\", \"0030\", \"0031\", \"0032\", \"0033\", \"0034\", \"0035\", \"0036\", \"0037\", \"0038\", \"0039\", \"0040\", \"0041\", \"0042\", \"0043\", \"0044\", \"0045\", \"0046\", \"0047\", \"0048\", \"0049\", \"0050\", \"0051\", \"0052\", \"0053\", \"0054\", \"0055\", \"0056\", \"0057\", \"0058\", \"0059\", \"0060\", \"0061\", \"0062\", \"0063\", \"0064\", \"0065\", \"0066\", \"0067\", \"0068\", \"0069\", \"0070\", \"0071\", \"0072\", \"0073\", \"0074\", \"0075\", \"0076\", \"0077\", \"0078\", \"0079\", \"0080\", \"0081\", \"0082\", \"0083\", \"0084\", \"0085\", \"0086\", \"0087\", \"0088\", \"0089\", \"0090\", \"0091\", \"0092\", \"0093\", \"0094\", \"0095\", \"0096\", \"0097\", \"0098\", \"0099\", \"0100\"], 0x561724b7cc20 /* 45 vars */) = 0\r\n163856 1582630469.904280 arch_prctl(0x1002, 0x7f49fca8c580) = 0\r\n163856 1582630469.904679 +++ exited with 0 +++\r\n163855 1582630469.903410 wait4(-1, 0x7fff442da620, 0, NULL) = 163856\r\n163855 1582630469.905400 +++ exited with 0 +++\r\n```\r\nTherefore original issue can be closed.\r\n\r\nBeside, maybe, documentation could have clarifying example (or at least mentioning), that `-v` and `-e verbose=` are independent, and you can abbreviate everything beside single syscall by using solely `-e verbose=execve`.\r\n\r\nHowever as a general enhancement, maybe there is still a sense to implement *per argument position* verbosity instead of only predetermined set of env, stat, termios anabled all at once. But maybe better not now :)",
