++  "body": "On Wed, Aug 05, 2020 at 02:33:08AM -0700, Alexandru Ardelean wrote:\n> For building with uclibc-ng, 2 modifications are required:\n> 1. adding `dirent.h` for PATH_MAX\n> 2. defining an IOV_MAX value if undefined (uclibc-ng doesn&#39;t seem to have this defined in limits.h)\n> \n> I&#39;ll admit that these fixes are not perfect, even half-assed.\n> But at least this can serve for some Google search to help others :)\n\nI'm sorry but no, this approach is not acceptable.\n\nIf you have a look for the latest edition of \"The Open Group Base\nSpecifications\" and check what it says about limits.h, you'll find\nthat both PATH_MAX and IOV_MAX shall be defined there.\n\nPlease bring this issue to attention of uclibc-ng developers as\nit's their responsibility to ensure that their library provides\nbasic POSIX.1-2008 compatibility.\n\nThanks.\n",
