++  "body": "On Mon, Oct 5, 2020 at 3:41 AM wangmu0579 <notifications@github.com> wrote:\n> I build v5.9 strace but stack-trace works on X86_64 with 64 binary taget but can't for 32 binary target.\n> How can I enable stack-trace for 32 binary target? Or any work-around for this?\n\nlibunwind is known to not work with binaries of non-strace-bitness;\nyou can try to use libdw-based unwinding (that is used in most\ndistributions where unwinding is enabled; `--with-libdw` configure\noption). Also, please check that mpers support is indeed enabled\n(`--enable-mpers=yes` configure option).  You can also refer to\n`strace -V` output for these build options.\n\n-- \nEugene Syromyatnikov\nmailto:evgsyr@gmail.com\nxmpp:esyr@jabber.{ru|org}\n",
