++  "updated_at": "2021-08-23T10:29:18Z",
++  "body": "> ```\r\n> git clone https://github.com/strace/strace\r\n> cd strace\r\n> ./bootstrap\r\n> ./configure\r\n> make LDFLAGS+='-static -pthread' CFLAGS+='-m32'\r\nPassing LDFLAGS/CFLAGS to make and not configure is wrong; moreover, proper build target setup for `configure` is missing.  This issue is due to improperly configured mpers/target and has nothing to do with static linking.\r\n\r\nThis works:\r\n```\r\n$ ./bootstrap && ./configure --build=i686-pc-linux-gnu --target=i686-pc-linux-gnu CC='gcc -m32' LDFLAGS='-static -pthread' && make -j16\r\n[...]\r\n$ file src/strace \r\nsrc/strace: ELF 32-bit LSB executable, Intel 80386, version 1 (GNU/Linux), statically linked, BuildID[sha1]=e744140daac6037ebcf7d52c47d73e063dc26570, for GNU/Linux 3.2.0, with debug_info, not stripped\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
