++  "body": "I tried building `strace 5.17` statically with `-k` (stack trace) option, using the following configure commands:\r\n\r\n```\r\n./configure LDFLAGS='-static -pthread' --enable-mpers=no --with-libunwind --with-libiberty\r\n```\r\n\r\nI get a similar error as mentioned in the previous comment: \r\n\r\n```\r\n...\r\nchecking for libunwind-ptrace.h... yes\r\nchecking for backtrace in -lunwind... no\r\nconfigure: error: in `/data/strace':\r\nconfigure: error: failed to find libunwind\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn `config.log`, the relevant part is:\r\n\r\n```\r\nconfigure:19308: checking for backtrace in -lunwind\r\nconfigure:19334: gcc -o conftest -g -O2  -I./bundled/linux/arch/x86/include/uapi -I./bundled/linux/include/uapi  -static -pthread  conftest.c -lunwind\r\n            >&5\r\n/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/7/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/libunwind.a(elf64.o): In function `xz_uncompressed_size':\r\n./src/elfxx.c:194: undefined reference to `lzma_stream_footer_decode'\r\n./src/elfxx.c:201: undefined reference to `lzma_index_buffer_decode'\r\n./src/elfxx.c:205: undefined reference to `lzma_index_size'\r\n./src/elfxx.c:210: undefined reference to `lzma_index_end'\r\n./src/elfxx.c:207: undefined reference to `lzma_index_uncompressed_size'\r\n./src/elfxx.c:210: undefined reference to `lzma_index_end'\r\n/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/7/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/libunwind.a(elf64.o): In function `_Uelf64_extract_minidebuginfo':\r\n./src/elfxx.c:278: undefined reference to `lzma_stream_buffer_decode'\r\ncollect2: error: ld returned 1 exit status\r\nconfigure:19334: $? = 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nI use Ubuntu 20.04 and I have installed `libunwind` using `sudo apt-get install libunwind-dev`.\r\n\r\nCould someone help me with this? Thanks!",
