++  "updated_at": "2022-09-17T12:15:48Z",
++  "body": "When a program is detected to be being debugged, the program may kill-9, and many programs will detect whether the current environment is being ptrace, and thus detect whether the current environment is a security hazard. \r\n\r\nIf the current environment is considered safe, the normal logic will continue. When this special case of detection, anti-debugging or ptrace, I did not find a good way to counter it.\r\n\r\nI don t know how the sandbox based on the seccomp implementation handles this kind of problem. Do you have any good suggestions, a great developer.",
