++  "body": "Fabrice, thanks for taking this on.  I'd like to ask you to follow the coding style we use in strace, which is similar to the one used in the Linux kernel.  In particular, tabs instead of spaces, `if (` instead of `if( `, and so on.  Also, I've already made most of automatic changes in the master branch, please rebase.  Please turn `TCP_STATE_*` macros into an `enum`, and add a comment about `TCP_STATE_DUMMY`, otherwise it's not clear why `tprint_or` is defined using `TCP_STATE_DUMMY` while `tprint_plus` is defined using `TCP_STATE_DELIM`.  I'll try to do a proper review when the code is updated.",
