++  "updated_at": "2023-02-06T09:04:49Z",
++  "body": "> I am currently working on a [pet project involving ptrace](https://github.com/i-ky/basset) and I would be very happy if there was some kind of library aiding in interpretation of `ptrace_syscall_info`. strace does that brilliantly (e.g. mapping syscall numbers to names for different architectures, extracting argument values), so it would be great if strace project shared some of its expertise with the world.\r\n> \r\n> I am willing to help, but I need to be pointed in the right direction.\r\n\r\nWith regards to this idea of creating a library out of strace, little has changed, we are essentially in the same situation as we were back in 2018: https://github.com/strace/strace/issues/70#issuecomment-392545240",
