++  "body": "> > I am also working on a project that would benefit from `strace`'s ability to decode argument system calls flawlessly independently of the architecture. We, for now, use `ptrace` and poke manually in some registers to decode arguments. Would be willing to help as well.\r\n> \r\n> Since we introduced the `PTRACE_GET_SYSCALL_INFO` API in the kernel, there is usually no need to deal with registers to decode syscalls.\r\n\r\nSure, but how about the system call arguments? We not only need pointers, but they actually decoded arguments, and I believe `strace` can do help there.",
