++  "body": "> I have added tests now. The data in the tests are collected from my GPU program and I used a script to generate the test functions.\r\n\r\nCan I see the script?\r\nI found /dev/kfd in my machine but I have no knowledge about it. So your script helps me.\r\n\r\n> ioctls that my GPU program does not call are now deleted and wont be addressed in this patchset due to a limited time budget. They have beed splitted to [kfd-dev branch](https://github.com/ZenithalHourlyRate/strace/tree/kfd-dev) and anyone interested could add tests for them and get them upstreamed.\r\n\r\nI would like to try to push your efforts to the upstream.\r\n\r\nThe parts of my patches were merged into ~the master~ ldv/next branch.\r\nHowever, the patches are a subset of what the kfd ioctl decoder needs.\r\nLinux kernel assigns the major number of kfd dynamically. The merged patches provide only major numbers to ioctl decoders.\r\n\r\nThese two patches are needed:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/masatake/strace/commit/2aa88bd278e0baee316045ab168d7157b8a4c144\r\nhttps://github.com/masatake/strace/commit/6bd09fea06f6369fe1c5f0d0a6431201f747d647\r\n\r\n@ldv-alt Should I use strace-list to get your review? or can I use this GitHub interface?\r\n",
