++  "body": "I've gone through the new finfo interface, there are some questions regarding how it can be used for kfd ioctl decoding\r\n\r\nIn `ioctl_decode`, `finfo` is NULL when it is leaving or the fd is not valid\r\n  * kfd and kd still needs distinguishing when in leaving stages\r\n  * in tests we are always using fd = -1\r\n\r\nThe leaving stage problem can be resolved by changing the logic in `SYS_FUNC(ioctl)`, but for the tests there are no way to provide finfo.\r\n\r\nIn summary, there must be some fallback ways to distinguish kfd and kd, and the code looks like this\r\n\r\n```\r\nif (finfo) {\r\n  // call kfd_ioctl or kd_ioctl accoring to the finfo\r\n} else {\r\n  if (_IOC_NR(code) >= _IOC_NR(KIOCSOUND))\r\n  // ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd the current ugly hack can not be avoided.\r\n\r\nSince we always need a fallback way, and there is actualy no overlap for now, I think kfd/kd distinguish can just use the hacky way for now to reduce the complexity. In the future when there are overlaps, finfo could be used. ",
