++  "updated_at": "2023-04-25T04:57:49Z",
++  "body": "True. It depends on how the tools are built. If the tool is built to do operations at high level/userspace, then the middlewares are responsible to convert them to into system compatible formats at runtime. In this case, strace is built in C & looking for systems calls at kernel space & these change depending on the kernel builds. Hence, I'm assuming this won't work for MacOS as the underlying systems & build are different.",
