++  "body": "> Executive summary [TL;DR]: Strace project was not friendly to me as a new contributor because of \"silly\" errors.\r\n> \r\n>     1. `make check` fails because `--enable-bundled=yes` is not configured.\r\n\r\nMaybe worth mentioning in the docs, but one usually don't have to use `--enable-bundled=yes` at all, you just happened to be unlucky to bump into an incompatible linux headers change a workaround for which had not been committed yet.\r\n\r\n>     2. `--enable-code-coverage` is omitted, yet is required of an accepted patch.\r\n\r\nIt is mentioned in dist/INSTALL, we use it for coverage builds only.\r\n\r\n>     3. Parallel `make` is not mentioned, but saves HOURS of time for `make check`.\r\n\r\nThis was addressed by commit 5afe61afd082d6fb7de6716bddd52bed9fb988e3, thanks.\r\n\r\n>     4. No `clang-format` style file in source, despite a call to follow coding style.\r\n\r\nThere seems to be no clang users here, so feel free to contribute one.\r\n\r\n>     5. No mention of the need to use a Debian-derived system to run workflow.\r\n\r\nThe CI workflow was written for github/gitlab, we don't use it elsewhere.",
