++  "body": "You are correct - my linux-6.3.2-rc2 toolchain has the following declaration.\r\n\r\n```\r\n/* argument for IORING_(UN)REGISTER_PBUF_RING */\r\nstruct io_uring_buf_reg {\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000__u64   ring_addr;\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000__u32   ring_entries;\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000__u16   bgid;\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000__u16   pad;\r\n\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000__u64   resv[3];\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\nbuild.LibreELEC-Generic.x86_64-12.0-devel$ find -name io_uring.h\r\n./build/linux-6.3.1/dest/include/linux/io_uring.h\r\n./build/linux-6.3.1/include/linux/io_uring.h\r\n./build/linux-6.3.1/include/trace/events/io_uring.h\r\n./build/linux-6.3.1/include/uapi/linux/io_uring.h\r\n./build/linux-6.3.1/usr/include/linux/io_uring.h\r\n./build/linux-6.3.1/io_uring/io_uring.h\r\n./build/strace-6.3/bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/io_uring.h\r\n./toolchain/x86_64-libreelec-linux-gnu/sysroot/usr/include/linux/io_uring.h\r\n```",
