++  "body": "Looks like the change in io_uring.h didn't make it in to Linux 6.3 so strace commit 65ecda71587 actually includes changes not in Linux 6.3 but the version check is still against 6.3 so the system headers are used instead of the bundled ones. I'm not sure if strace does maintenance releases but would reverting 65ecda71587 in a 6.3.1 be an option? Forcing use of bundled headers is a reasonable workaround but that requires downstream packagers to change their build scripts. From a ct-ng point of view we'll probably just wait until 6.4.",
