++  "body": "Hi @masatake . I'm a bit stuck with writing a test, could you please help me out with that?\r\n\r\nThe test i have in mind is very simple: \r\n1. let's run strace with a very low stacktrace-frames-limit, like 1, and ensure we have the \"too many stack frames\" in the output\r\n2. let's run the same test without the limit and ensure we don't have the phrase in the output\r\n\r\nThis doesn't really check that the limit could go above the default, but it definitely checks that the limit is configurable, and i think this is good enough.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nI'd like to reuse `strace-k.test` for that to not copy-paste the attaching process, but the `awk` scripts in it look like arcane magic for my untrained eye, so could you please suggest what would be the easiest way to do what i want?",
