++  "body": "Do you think  this is a CLEAR example of how to run strace? \r\n\r\n```\r\n      strace [-ACdffhikqqrtttTvVwxxyyYzZ] [-a column] [-b execve]\r\n              [-e expr]... [-I n] [-o file] [-O overhead] [-p pid]...\r\n              [-P path]... [-s strsize] [-S sortby] [-U columns]\r\n              [-X format] [--seccomp-bpf] [--syscall-limit limit]\r\n              [--secontext[=format]] [--tips[=format]] { -p pid | [-DDD]\r\n              [-E var[=val]]... [-u username] command [args] }\r\n```\r\ncompare to this:\r\n`strace options  ./program options` \r\n\r\nAnd what means command? It is very arguable what that means. A command can be any character typed somewhere (valid or invalid). program / app is much clearer i think! \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
