++  "body": "> Very simple addition as I noticed the Lustre distributed filesystem magic codes were not present in the defined values.\r\n\r\nWhere do these constants come from?  They are not defined in the Linux kernel tree nowadays, and before the removal there was just LL_SUPER_MAGIC defined to 0x0BD00BD0 somewhere deep in the staging area. glibc doesn't provide them either, but internally uses just LUSTRE_SUPER_MAGIC defined to 0x0BD00BD0.  Given this level of obscurity and contradictions, I'm not sure providing these symbolic constants in strace would be helpful.",
