++  "body": "https://github.com/strace/strace/blob/master/doc/strace.1.in is the file you must update.\r\n\r\nconfigure generates strace.1 from it. You can review the page with man command like: \r\n```\r\n$ man ./doc/strace.1\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou can start your work like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndiff --git a/doc/strace.1.in b/doc/strace.1.in\r\nindex 37e2c38bd..2935ab86a 100644\r\n--- a/doc/strace.1.in\r\n+++ b/doc/strace.1.in\r\n@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@ strace \\- trace system calls and signals\r\n .OP \\-U columns\r\n .OP \\-X format\r\n .OP \\-\\-seccomp\\-bpf\r\n+.OP \\-\\-stacktrace\\-frames\\-limit limit\r\n .OP \\-\\-syscall\\-limit limit\r\n .if '@ENABLE_SECONTEXT_FALSE@'#' .OP \\-\\-secontext\\fR[=\\fIformat\\fR]\r\n .OP \\-\\-tips\\fR[=\\fIformat\\fR]\r\n```\r\n\r\nAbout the syntax, you can find hints in https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/groff_man.7.html. \r\n",
