++  "updated_at": "2024-01-30T23:13:36Z",
++  "body": "The [Julia project](https://julialang.org/) has [built `strace` v6.7 binaries](https://github.com/JuliaBinaryWrappers/strace_jll.jl/releases/tag/strace-v6.7.0%2B1) as part of its [Yggdrasil community build tree](https://github.com/JuliaPackaging/Yggdrasil/blob/master/S/strace/build_tarballs.jl). While these are not static builds, they are built against a [reasonably old glibc](https://github.com/JuliaPackaging/Yggdrasil/blob/master/RootFS.md#glibc-versions) and meant for wide distribution, so they should work just about anywhere.  You should be able to directly download one of the tarballs in that GitHub release, unpack it and run it directly.\r\n\r\nThe reason they're not static is because when I statically linked `glibc` into the `strace` binary, I got the dreaded error\r\n```\r\nstrace: loadlocale.c:130: _nl_intern_locale_data: Assertion `cnt < (sizeof (_nl_value_type_LC_TIME) / sizeof (_nl_value_type_LC_TIME[0]))' failed.\r\n```\r\nWhich, as far as I can tell, is just a bug in my old version of `glibc` that I'm triggering because I'm using an ancient glibc version on a newer machine.",
