++  "updated_at": "2024-02-17T20:51:52Z",
++  "body": "> Is there a standard way to run only a subset of tests?\r\n\r\nSince we use a traditional automake based test driver, something as simple as\r\n```\r\nmake -k check TESTS='ioctl_v4l2.gen.test ioctl_v4l2-success.gen.test'\r\n```\r\nwould do.\r\n\r\n> `make check TESTS='*v4l2*'` fails with many messages like:\r\n\r\nThat kind of globbing grabs unrelated files, try something like\r\n```\r\nmake -s check TESTS='ioctl_v4l2*.gen.test'\r\n```\r\nor, if the build is in a subdirectory,\r\n```\r\nmake -s check TESTS=\"$(ls ../../tests/ioctl_v4l2*.gen.test |sed 's/.*\\///')\"\r\n```",
