++  "body": "Tested the fix and looks like it is OK\r\n\r\n> strace has to support building and running on much older kernels than 6.8.\r\n\r\nIMO expecting trat strace X.X will be OK for older kernel version is kind of wrong because it will automatically have impact on complexity of the strace code.\r\nIMO it would be good to add such policy on maintaining strace code because it would allow drop some legacy code.\r\nIf it will be any critical bug which should be fixed with updated version it is always possible to add branch on top of exact version tag and add necessary fixes only in that branch.\r\n\r\nNevertheless looks like last 6.8 is OK for older kernel versions and not well suited for last kernel 6.8.x.\r\n",
