++  "body": "- I'm a bit wary of having such a behaviour change by default and non-optional: it would be nice to have an option to at least opt out of it (without disabling other decoding features), since parsing the arg as a pointer and displaying it as a string may obscure the possibly more desired arg value (since we try to decode ioctls we have no idea about).  A possible user interface for controlling the behaviour could be `-e ioctl=hexdump-unknown-arg`;  I don't have a strong preference about (not) making it the default, however.\r\n- It probably makes sense to have the same behaviour for printing unknown commands for known ioctl types as well.",
