++  "body": "`strace` has options to make it's output more verbose which can be incredibly useful for debugging and clarity, however, this often makes lots of syscalls output lines which are longer than the terminal width.\n\nthe current behaviour is that strace simply does not tackle this and the lines are overflown by the terminal. This makes it hard to parse the output visually, as the syscall invocations are interleaved with the overflown lines. I wish that strace queried the width of the terminal, and broke the new lines and indented them itself, to make the output easier to parse.\n\nSomething like this:\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"860\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1a014bea-e0a5-40cf-bf9a-5cbce1454fe0\" />\n\nThis may be undesirable for greppability and non-terminal output, so it would be gated behind a CLI flag.\n\nI'd be down to give implementing this a shot, if you think this makes sense.",
