++  "body": "When setns is called with nstype specified as 0, any type of namespace\r\ncan be joined and the type is determined by the passed fd. Query the\r\nnamespace type of the fd by reading the /proc/$pid/fd/$fd symlink to\r\nretrieve the type of namespace being joined.\r\n\r\n* NEWS: Mention this change.\r\n* src/clone.c (read_namespace_type_for_fd): New helper function.\r\n(get_namespace_auxstr): Add expected_ns_str parameter.\r\nIf flags is 0, print the namespace ID of expected_ns_str.\r\n(SYS_FUNC(clone), SYS_FUNC(clone3), SYS_FUNC(unshare)): Pass NULL\r\nas expected_ns_str to get_namespace_auxstr.\r\n(SYS_FUNC(setns)): Query the namespace type of the joined fd\r\nusing read_namespace_type_for_fd if nstype is 0, and pass it as\r\nexpected_ns_str to get_namespace_auxstr.\r\n* tests/setns-report-ns-id.c (main): Add a test case for setns(fd, 0).\r\n\r\nAssisted-by: Antigravity:Gemini-3.5-Flash (comit log)\r\n",
