++  "body": "## Environment\n\n- strace 6.8\n- Linux 6.17.0-35-generic x86_64\n- Ubuntu 24.04.1\n- glibc 2.39, GCC 13.3.0\n\n## Description\n\n`strace -c` segfaults during summary printing with certain syscall patterns. The traced program completes successfully (body written, exit 0), but strace itself crashes with SIGSEGV in `__strlen_avx2` when generating the summary after the child exits.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/anomalyco/curldbg.git\ncd curldbg\nmake\npython3 tests/server.py &\nstrace -c ./curldbg -s -o /dev/null http://127.0.0.1:9999/get\n```\n\nExpected: summary table printed, exit 0. Actual: segfault, exit 139.\n\nThe crash is **not in the traced program**:\n- `strace` without `-c` works fine (shows `+++ exited with 0 +++`)\n- `strace -C` works fine\n- The body is written correctly before strace segfaults\n\n## Heap-layout dependent\n\nThe same binary with identical flags to an HTTPS target works fine, confirming the crash depends on memory layout:\n\n```\n# Works (exit 0, 233 syscalls):\nstrace -c ./curldbg -s -o /dev/null https://httpbin.org/get\n\n# Crashes (exit 139, ~200 syscalls):\nstrace -c ./curldbg -s -o /dev/null http://127.0.0.1:9999/get\n```\n\nThe TLS code path loads libssl/libcrypto which shifts heap layout and avoids the corruption. Without TLS, the bug manifests 100% of the time.\n\n## Backtrace\n\n```\n(gdb) bt\n#0  __strlen_avx2 () at ../sysdeps/x86_64/multiarch/strlen-avx2.S:76\n#1  0x00005555555e5f66 in strace summary-printing code\n#2  0x00007ffff7c2a1ca in __libc_start_call_main\n```\n\n## Additional notes\n\n- `strace -c -e trace=close ./curldbg ...` also crashes (only tracing close + exit_group is enough)\n- The crash occurs during `exit_group` processing when strace formats its internal summary table\n- It appears to be a NULL or corrupted string pointer being passed to `strlen()` by strace's own data structures\n\n## Workaround\n\nUse `strace -C` instead of `strace -c` for collecting the summary.",
