++  "body": "Linux fixed  timespec64 definition in _90079798f1d7 (\"delayacct: fix uapi timespec64 definition\")_ and since then `linux/taskstats.h` needs `linux/time_types.h`. This change was brought into strace with 33b9507, which didn't add `linux/time_types.h` so the build fails with:\n```\nIn file included from ../bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/cgroupstats.h:20,\n                 from netlink_nlctrl.c:11:\n../bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/taskstats.h:21:10: fatal error: linux/time_types.h: No such file or directory\n   21 | #include <linux/time_types.h>\n      |          ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\nSorry for not providing PR right away; `linux/time_types.h` needs `__kernel_old_time_t`:\n```\nIn file included from ../bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/taskstats.h:21,\n                 from ../bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/cgroupstats.h:20,\n                 from netlink_nlctrl.c:11:\n../bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/time_types.h:32:9: error: unknown type name '__kernel_old_time_t'; did you mean '__kernel_old_gid_t'?\n   32 |         __kernel_old_time_t     tv_sec;         /* seconds */\n      |         ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n      |         __kernel_old_gid_t\n```\nThat's in `asm/posix_types.h` included through `linux/types.h`, but despite later is in tree for a long time, the former is not, thus I wonder how is `--enable-bundled` supposed to work.",
