++  "body": "Both the latest LTS (r27d) and latest stable (r29) NDK versions produce the same error.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n```\ngit clone https://github.com/strace/strace.git\ncd strace\n./bootstrap\n\nNDK_PATH=/path/to/ndk\nTOOLCHAIN=\"${NDK_PATH}/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64\"\nexport CC=\"${TOOLCHAIN}/bin/aarch64-linux-android35-clang\"\nexport AR=\"${TOOLCHAIN}/bin/llvm-ar\"\nexport RANLIB=\"${TOOLCHAIN}/bin/llvm-ranlib\"\nexport STRIP=\"${TOOLCHAIN}/bin/llvm-strip\"\n./configure --host=aarch64-linux-android35 --target=aarch64-linux-android35 --disable-mpers --disable-gcc-Werror\nmake\n```\n\nThe build will fail with the following error:\n```\n/path/to/ndk/toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64/bin/../sysroot/usr/include/arpa/inet.h:40:1: error: unknown type name 'in_addr_t'\n   40 | in_addr_t inet_addr(const char* _Nonnull __s);\n      | ^\n```\n\nA workaround I found is to set `export CFLAGS=\"-Din_addr_t=uint32_t\"`.",
