++  "body": "@ldv-alt I'm very sorry to make a pull request just after you merged #345.\r\n\r\nHowever, I found a limitation in #345 that we cannot ignore.\r\n\r\nI have tried the merged version of strace with the tracee available at https://github.com/masatake/kernel-essential-training/blob/master/kvm/add-iomem-kvm.c.\r\nadd-iomem-kvm.c demonstrates device emulation via I/O memory.\r\n\r\nThe tracee reads data from the address that has no memory-mapping.\r\nIn such a case, the tracee gains control with KVM_EXIT_IOMEM.\r\nThe tracee provides data via `run->mmio.data[0] = ` here `run` points memory region where kvm_run is mapped. Then the tracee invokes ioctl(KVM_RUN) to enter the guest mode.\r\n\r\nI proposed `VCPU> ` in #345; strace mainly decoded the after-state of the kvm_run structure.\r\nThough I considered decoding the difference between the before-state and after-state using tprint_value_changed, I found that my code was insufficient. I assumed exit_reason didn't change between the before-state and the after-state. e.g., When the guest exits with KVM_EXIT_IO, strace cannot decode the value of run->mmio.data[0] because the handler for KVM_EXIT_IOMEM decodes run->mmio.data[0].\r\n\r\nIn this pull request, I propose `VCPU< ` for decoding before-state and `VCPU> ` for decoding after-state.\r\n\r\n```console\r\nioctl(5, KVM_RUN, 0)                    = 0 (KVM_EXIT_IO)\r\n VCPU:0< {..., exit_reason=6 /* KVM_EXIT_MMIO */, ..., {mmio={..., data=[0x3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0], len=1, is_write=0}}}\r\n VCPU:0> {..., exit_reason=2 /* KVM_EXIT_IO */, ..., {io={...}}}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThank you for reading.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
