++  "body": "Hi,\n\nWhen running the testsuite on systems where there is no vDSO, the glibc malloc implementation might issue some `clock_gettime64`. It used to be fairly rare, but a [recent glibc patch](https://sourceware.org/git/?p=glibc.git;a=commit;h=a96a82c4a5efd3139e75cd11fd2a5554164dd5a0) made this much more likely. As a result we've started seeing [testsuite failures](https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/glibc/+bug/2125424) on Ubuntu armhf builders.\n\nI wrote a [workaround](https://git.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/strace/tree/debian/patches/0004-Erase-clock_gettime64-calls-on-armhf.patch?h=import/6.16%2bds-2ubuntu2) to unblock the Ubuntu side, and I still don't know if the absence of vDSO is deliberate or not. If so, though, it's not a great long term solution, and in any case I figure I'd get the word out in case somebody else has similar issues.",
