++  "body": "Building strace fails when using glibc version 2.41. The error is caused by a conflicting definition of `struct sched_attr` between strace's bundled Linux headers and the system's glibc headers.\n\n### Error snippet:\n```\nIn file included from sched.c:14:\n../bundled/linux/include/uapi/linux/sched/types.h:98:8: error: redefinition of 'struct sched_attr'\n   98 | struct sched_attr {\n      |        ^~~~~~~~~~\nIn file included from /x86_64-cross-linux-gnu/sys-root/include/sched.h:43,\n                 from sched.c:13:\n/x86_64-cross-linux-gnu/sys-root/lib64/gcc/x86_64-cross-linux-gnu/11.5.0/include-fixed/bits/sched.h:80:8: note: originally defined here\n   80 | struct sched_attr\n      |        ^~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\n### Root cause:\nThe `struct sched_attr` is now defined in glibc 2.41's headers, but strace also includes its own bundled Linux kernel headers which define the same struct, leading to a redefinition error.\n\n### Environment:\nstrace version: 6.16\nglibc version: 2.41\nCompiler: gcc 11.5.0\nSystem: Linux x86_64",
