++  "body": "We (yoctoproject.org) run the strace test suite and have noticed that a number of tests are sensitive to system load and occasionally fail.\n\nWe're currently skipping clock_nanosleep, delay, nanosleep, and strace-r.\n\nFrom experience I group load-sensitive tests into three categories:\n1) Genuinely sensitive to load because the test has timeouts that need to be low, so the test _must_ run on idle and fast systems. This means the tests will fail when ran on busy systems, or particularly slow systems (be it a raspberrypi1, or a slow qemu). In general I suggest having a way to skip tests that depend on a fast/idle system.\n\n2) Tests sensitive to load because the test has timeouts that are low for no good reason, eg using 100ms when the task being waited for could take 120ms. In this case there's no reason not to bump the timeout to something higher (like 10s) to cater for slow/busy systems.\n\n3) Tests with race conditions that mostly are not noticable. These should be fixed.\n\nI've not yet dug into what categories the tests we're having to skip are, but I wanted to file this ticket to raise it with the strace maintainers to see if you have any thoughts.",
