++  "body": "When running the test suite on a system with musl-libc, the uio test fails:\n\n```\nFailed patterns of expected output:\n#3: pwrite(64)?\\(0, \"\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0\", 4, 1004211379570065135\\) += 4\n#4: pwritev\\(0, \\[\\{iov_base=\"\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0\\\\0\", iov_len=4\\}\\], 1, 1004211379570065135\\) += 4\n\nActual output:\nmmap(0x56381027a000, 4096, PROT_NONE, MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_FIXED|MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0) = 0x56381027a000\nclose(0)                                = 0\nopen(\"/dev/zero\", O_RDONLY|O_LARGEFILE) = 0\npread64(0, \"\\0\\0\\0\\0\", 4, 1004211379570065135) = 4\npreadv(0, [{iov_base=\"\\0\\0\\0\\0\", iov_len=4}], 1, 1004211379570065135) = 4\nclose(0)                                = 0\nopen(\"/dev/null\", O_WRONLY|O_LARGEFILE) = 0\npwritev2(0, [{iov_base=\"\\0\\0\\0\\0\", iov_len=4}], 1, 1004211379570065135, RWF_NOAPPEND) = 4\npwritev2(0, [{iov_base=\"\\0\\0\\0\\0\", iov_len=4}], 1, 1004211379570065135, RWF_NOAPPEND) = 4\nclose(0)                                = 0\n+++ exited with 0 +++\nuio.test: failed test: ../../src/strace -e%desc ../uio output mismatch\nFAIL uio.test (exit status: 1)\n```\n\nThe reason seems to be the way musl handles the pwrite calls: both `pwrite` and `pwritev` are actually `pwritev2`:\ncalling `pwrite` calls `pwritev2`: https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/tree/src/unistd/pwrite.c#n10\ncalling `pwritev` calls `pwritev2`: https://git.musl-libc.org/cgit/musl/tree/src/unistd/pwritev.c#n10\n",
