++  "body": "strace has `-e kvm=vcpu` already.\r\nThis pull request extends the option.\r\nThis pull request adds `-e kvm=vcpu+` option.\r\nThe new option is for ~dumping~ decoding the kvm_run mmap'ed area.\r\n```console\r\n[yamato@dev64]~/var/strace/tests% ../src/strace -y -e ioctl -e kvm=vcpu+ ./ioctl_kvm_run_auxstr_vcpu\r\n...\r\nioctl(5<anon_inode:kvm-vcpu:0>, KVM_RUN, 0) = 0 (KVM_EXIT_IO)\r\nVCPU>{request_interrupt_window=0, immediate_exit=0, \r\nVCPU+ exit_reason=2 (KVM_EXIT_IO), ready_for_interrupt_injection=0, if_flag=0, flags=0, \r\nVCPU+ cr8=0000000000000000, apic_base=0000000000000000 => 0x000000fee00900, \r\nVCPU+ {io={direction=KVM_EXIT_IO_OUT, port=0x3f8, count=1, data_offset=0x00000000001000}}}\r\nioctl(5<anon_inode:kvm-vcpu:0>, KVM_RUN, 0) = 0 (KVM_EXIT_HLT)\r\nVCPU>{request_interrupt_window=0, immediate_exit=0, \r\nVCPU+ exit_reason=5 (KVM_EXIT_HLT), ready_for_interrupt_injection=0, if_flag=0, flags=0, \r\nVCPU+ cr8=0000000000000000, apic_base=0x000000fee00900}\r\n+++ exited with 0 +++\r\n```\r\n\r\nVCPU> and VCPU+ are the prefixes for the ~dump~ decoded data.\r\n",
