++  "body": "This is for the `--decode-fds=all` option. Currently after a unix socket gets bind()ed a name:\n```\nbind(103<UNIX:[1629885]>, {sa_family=0x1 /* AF_UNIX */, sun_path=@\"my-neat-socket\\x00\\x00\\x00\"}, 110 <unfinished ...>\n```\nthat name is not shown in other syscalls involving that fd:\n```\nlisten(103<UNIX:[1629885]>, 4 <unfinished ...>\n```\nThis would be useful because when analyzing a binary you may want to search for all syscalls involving operations on a given socket, and the name of the socket stays consistent between program runs (or if the socket is destroyed/recreated).",
