++  "body": "Currently, the `-e trace=%desc` option is documented simply as \u201ctrace file descriptor-related syscalls\u201d. The same happens for other sets like `%proc` or `%memory`. It would be helpful for users if the man page also pointed to the underlying system calls.\n\nI found that the information is platform specific, for example in `strace/src/linux/arm/syscallent.h`:\n\n```c\n// ...\n[ 60] = { 1,\tNF,\t\tSEN(umask),\t\t\t\"umask\"\t\t\t},\n[ 61] = { 1,\tTF,\t\tSEN(chroot),\t\t\t\"chroot\"\t\t},\n[ 62] = { 2,\tTSFA,\t\tSEN(ustat),\t\t\t\"ustat\"\t\t\t},\n[ 63] = { 2,\tTD,\t\tSEN(dup2),\t\t\t\"dup2\"\t\t\t},\n[ 64] = { 0,\tPU|NF,\t\tSEN(getppid),\t\t\t\"getppid\"\t\t},\n[ 65] = { 0,\tPU|NF,\t\tSEN(getpgrp),\t\t\t\"getpgrp\"\t\t},\n// ...\n```\n\n",
