++  "body": "Hello @ldv-alt! \n\nI would like to document the project so that it has a clear documentation and one simply looks into it and understands the main ideas behind the framework. So let's start with main() function. We have dispatch/emit event inside of an eternal loop. How would you describe what the loop does in plain words? Does strace use ptrace system call under the hood?\n\nI am just checking if you would answer my issue because it seems that you didn't answer my email. So I thought that you probably missed that and it's better to proceed in public here on GitHub because the history of the conversation is going to be stored. So as I said, I am going to ask more questions to clarify the operation of strace overall. Let's do it in this thread and then maybe if something is good enough to be included in the documentation, we can do that. I am talking about something like architectural overview of how strace works.\n\nThanks.\n\nP. S.: I am trying to port strace to FreeBSD and my goal is to pick the smallest stack available so that I can start working towards having something reasonable as a result. Namely, I am interested in parsing netlink messages. So if you show up in this thread, @ldv-alt , then I will ask more clear questions about that.",
