++  "body": "Hello.\r\n\r\nI'm thinking either I'm misunderstanding the meaning of the --summary-only report, or strace is having a bad time of it.\r\n\r\nI'm seeing:\r\n$ strace --summary-only /bin/sleep 10\r\nbelow cmd output started 2024 Fri Sep 27 02:22:33 PM PDT\r\n% time     seconds  usecs/call     calls    errors syscall\r\n------ ----------- ----------- --------- --------- ----------------\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           read\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         4           close\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         8           mmap\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         4           mprotect\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           munmap\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         3           brk\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         4           pread64\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1         1 access\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           execve\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         2         1 arch_prctl\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           set_tid_address\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           clock_nanosleep\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         2           openat\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         2           newfstatat\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           set_robust_list\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           prlimit64\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           getrandom\r\n  0.00    0.000000           0         1           rseq\r\n------ ----------- ----------- --------- --------- ----------------\r\n100.00    0.000000           0        39         2 total\r\nabove cmd output done    2024 Fri Sep 27 02:22:43 PM PDT\r\n\r\nI would've expected clock_nanosleep() to be 10 seconds.\r\n\r\nWhat am I missing?\r\n\r\nI'm using: strace -- version 5.16\r\n...on a Linux system.\r\n\r\nThanks for the great tool!  It's one of the main things I miss when I use a Mac.\r\n\r\nPS: I started suspecting something was misunderstood or broken when a test program reported strange results with strace --summary-only too.\r\n",
