++  "body": "Distro packages for strace seem to disable the test suite on riscv64 (see for example [Fedora](http://fedora.riscv.rocks:3000/rpms/strace/src/commit/37fbe25da5896569c05efd0f2b8c4f01010bbe87/strace.spec#L109-L113) and [Debian](https://salsa.debian.org/debian/strace/-/blob/b225a340e2af5fe0cbe035cebb08738eb6b88da8/debian/rules#L59-63)).\r\n\r\nI recently tried building the latest Fedora package on riscv64 with test suite enabled and it mostly worked fine, with the exception of a single failure for `tests/legacy_syscall_info.test`. Minimal reproducer that displays the issue:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ ./src/strace /\r\nexecve(\"/\", [\"/\"], 0x3fd7194e00 /* 35 vars */) = -1 EACCES (Permission denied)\r\n./src/strace: exec: Permission denied\r\n+++ exited with 1 +++\r\n\r\n$ ./src/disable_ptrace_get_syscall_info ./src/strace /\r\nexecve(0xffffffffffffffda, [\"/\"], 0x3fe6949df0 /* 35 vars */) = -1 EACCES (Permission denied)\r\n./src/strace: exec: Permission denied\r\n+++ exited with 1 +++\r\n```\r\n\r\nNo matter what program is run under strace and which syscalls it uses, the first argument to any syscall is always reported as `0xffffffffffffffda` when `PTRACE_GET_SYSCALL_INFO` is not available. All the other argument are fine.\r\n\r\nI've sprinkled `tprintf_string()` all over the place, notably in `ptrace_setregset()`, and based on what I've seen it's not some code in strace itself that causes the bogus value to be reported: if I inspect `riscv_regs.a0` immediately after calling `strace()`, I can see that the previous value has been overwritten by the syscall.\r\n\r\nSo either there's a bug in the kernel, or strace needs to do something different to get the actual value of `a0`. Looking at the kernel source I can see that an [`orig_a0`](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/196145c606d0f816fd3926483cb1ff87e09c2c0b/arch/riscv/include/asm/ptrace.h#L52-L53) field exists in `struct pt_regs`, but AFAICT that's private data that we can't get access to from userspace...\r\n\r\nI'm afraid this is as far as I'm able to go. Please let me know if I can provide additional information, test tentative patches, or do anything else to help get this fixed.",
