++  "body": "Hi, not sure what causes this yet, but I'm trying to build `strace` in an `alpine:3.20` based docker container, and I'm hitting this roadblock:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nc096207374f1:/tmp/strace# ./bootstrap\r\ngenerating ./src/xlat/x86_xfeatures.h\r\ngenerating ./src/xlat/xattrflags.h\r\ngenerating ./src/xlat/xdp_flags.h\r\ngenerating ./src/xlat/xdp_sockaddr_flags.h\r\ngenerating ./src/xlat/xfs_dqblk_flags.h\r\ngenerating ./src/xlat/xfs_quota_flags.h\r\ngenerating ./src/xlat/.gitignore\r\ngenerating ./src/xlat/Makemodule.am\r\ndate: invalid date 'Tue, 13 Aug 2024 16:16:14 +0000'\r\ndate: invalid date 'Sun, 30 Jun 2024 08:00:00 +0000'\r\n./build-aux/file-date-gen: Invalid date: Sun, 30 Jun 2024 08:00:00 +0000\r\nconfigure.ac:21: error: assert failed: 1 == 0\r\nm4/st_esyscmd_s.m4:8: st_esyscmd_s is expanded from...\r\nconfigure.ac:21: the top level\r\nautom4te: error: /usr/bin/m4 failed with exit status: 1\r\naclocal: error: /usr/bin/autom4te failed with exit status: 1\r\nautoreconf: error: aclocal failed with exit status: 1\r\nc096207374f1:/tmp/strace# date\r\nThu Aug 15 10:08:23 UTC 2024\r\n```\r\n\r\nAny ideas what causes this or how to fix this?",
