++  "body": "Hi!\r\nI see there is a [cache of symbolization results](https://github.com/strace/strace/blob/ab728c1fc04eef9629fce1835f39ab0460ebd245/src/unwind-libdw.c#L28) when strace is built with libdw, however it's not the case for libunwind.\r\n\r\nGiven that the overhead difference of `-k` option between strace-libdw and strace-libunwind is immense due to the cache in question, and that Ubuntu/Debian packages strace with libunwind for amd64, would it make sense to cache the symbolization results for libunwind-based stack tracing as well?",
