++  "body": "The kernel processes the fifth system call argument of `mremap` if `MREMAP_DONTUNMAP` is passed (and not just for `MREMAP_FIXED`). I would appreciate if `strace` could print that, too.  Something like:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/src/mem.c b/src/mem.c\r\nindex 80e3ba706..2612e39a2 100644\r\n--- a/src/mem.c\r\n+++ b/src/mem.c\r\n@@ -279,8 +279,9 @@ SYS_FUNC(mremap)\r\n        /* flags */\r\n        printflags64(mremap_flags, tcp->u_arg[3], \"MREMAP_???\");\r\n \r\n-       if ((tcp->u_arg[3] & (MREMAP_MAYMOVE | MREMAP_FIXED)) ==\r\n-           (MREMAP_MAYMOVE | MREMAP_FIXED)) {\r\n+       if (((tcp->u_arg[3] & (MREMAP_MAYMOVE | MREMAP_FIXED)) ==\r\n+            (MREMAP_MAYMOVE | MREMAP_FIXED)) ||\r\n+           tcp->u_arg[3] & MREMAP_DONTUNMAP) {\r\n                /* new_address */\r\n                tprint_arg_next();\r\n                printaddr(tcp->u_arg[4]);\r\n```",
