++  "body": "There are a few strace -k test failures when building strace 6.9 with libdw on aarch64 systems with pointer authentication on. This is similar but different to #12, which was about tests failing when strace is built with libunwind.\r\n\r\nBuilding strace 6.9 with libdw, I get the following (correct) output on a aarch64 system without pointer authentication. This can be either a CPU that does not support pointer authentication at all, or a machine booted with the feature disabled (ie. booting the kernel with `arm64.nopauth`):\r\n\r\n```\r\n (sid_arm64-dchroot)ema@amdahl:~/strace-6.9$ ./build/src/strace -e chdir -k build/tests/stack-fcall\r\n chdir(\"\")                               = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)\r\n  > /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6(chdir+0xc) [0xdf48c]\r\n  > /home/ema/strace-6.9/build/tests/stack-fcall(f3+0xbb) [0xb9b]\r\n  > /home/ema/strace-6.9/build/tests/stack-fcall(f2+0x67) [0xa87]\r\n  > /home/ema/strace-6.9/build/tests/stack-fcall(f1+0x67) [0x9c7]\r\n  > /home/ema/strace-6.9/build/tests/stack-fcall(f0+0x67) [0x907]\r\n[...]\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn a system with pointer authentication turned on, instead, the (wrong) output is:\r\n```\r\n (sid-arm64-sbuild)ema@virna:~/packages/strace-6.9$ ./build/src/strace -e chdir -k build/tests/stack-fcall\r\n chdir(\"\")                               = -1 ENOENT (No such file or directory)\r\n  > /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6(chdir+0xc) [0xdf48c]\r\n  > /home/ema/packages/strace-6.9/build/tests/stack-fcall(f3+0xbb) [0xb9b]\r\n  > /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1() [0x59aaab3ca7da87]\r\n  > /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1() [0x59aaab3ca7da87]\r\n  > /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/ld-linux-aarch64.so.1() [0x6faaab3ca7d9c7]\r\n[...]\r\n```\r\n\r\n",
