++  "body": "strace help page do not EXPLICITY says that output to filename must be set exactly after strace, and not at the end of the command.\r\n\r\nIf you search in stackoverflow / superusers, many have problems to understand that --output=log.txt must be set exactly AFTER strace and not at the end of the full command in terminal\r\n\r\nRight: strace --output=log.txt ./program\r\nWrong (no output file): strace  ./program --output=log.txt\r\n\r\nEven my self now more than 15 minutes tried to understand why a log file was not produced experimenting with many combinations! Please edit your man page to be clearer on that topic.",
