++  "body": "This program\r\n\r\n```c\r\n#define _XOPEN_SOURCE 700\r\n#include <termios.h>\r\n\r\nint main()\r\n{\r\n    struct termios t;\r\n\r\n    // assume we're being run from a terminal and fd 0 is a TTY/PTY\r\n    tcgetattr(0, &t);\r\n    t.c_cflag |= CLOCAL;\r\n    tcsetattr(0, TCSANOW, &t);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nPrints the following trace:\r\n\r\n```\r\nioctl(0, TCGETS, {c_iflag=ICRNL|IXON|IUTF8, c_oflag=NL0|CR0|TAB0|BS0|VT0|FF0|OPOST|ONLCR, c_cflag=B38400|CS8|CREAD, c_lflag=ISIG|ICANON|ECHO|ECHOE|ECHOK|IEXTEN|ECHOCTL|ECHOKE, ...}) = 0\r\nioctl(0, TCGETS, {c_iflag=ICRNL|IXON|IUTF8, c_oflag=NL0|CR0|TAB0|BS0|VT0|FF0|OPOST|ONLCR, c_cflag=B38400|CS8|CREAD, c_lflag=ISIG|ICANON|ECHO|ECHOE|ECHOK|IEXTEN|ECHOCTL|ECHOKE, ...}) = 0\r\nioctl(0, TCSETS, {c_iflag=ICRNL|IXON|IUTF8, c_oflag=NL0|CR0|TAB0|BS0|VT0|FF0|OPOST|ONLCR, c_cflag=B38400|CS8|CREAD|CLOCAL, c_lflag=ISIG|ICANON|ECHO|ECHOE|ECHOK|IEXTEN|ECHOCTL|ECHOKE, ...}) = 0\r\nioctl(0, TCGETS, {c_iflag=ICRNL|IXON|IUTF8, c_oflag=NL0|CR0|TAB0|BS0|VT0|FF0|OPOST|ONLCR, c_cflag=B38400|CS8|CREAD|CLOCAL, c_lflag=ISIG|ICANON|ECHO|ECHOE|ECHOK|IEXTEN|ECHOCTL|ECHOKE, ...}) = 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nEven though the source code for tcgetattr/tcsetattr in glibc definitely only fires a single ioctl respectively.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if this is a bug (in both cases, the extra print is for TCGETS), or if something more nefarious is going on (as far as I'm aware, there's no symbol interposition happening and I don't think there's any other way to 'listen' for terminal attribute changes)",
