++  "body": "I'm currently trying to write a script which shows which file is edit by a process and it's childs. You can filter the output by the process. I'm using `strace -fyy -e trace=%file --decode-pids=comm <command>` and parse the output.  But there's a little problem: If a syscall is made by a child process, strace prints `[pid  {pid}<{name}>] {rest of line}`, but if the syscall is made by the process started by strace, this part if missing, what makes this more complex to parse. It would be nice to have a argument to make the output always starts with  `[pid  {pid}<{name}>] {rest of line}`.",
