++  "body": "As mentioned in https://github.com/sunlin7/compile-db-gen/issues/2, adding `--seccomp-bpf` can result in a huge performance improvement. Why not enable it by default?\r\n\r\nI understand, that there may be corner cases, when `--seccomp-bpf` has undesirable effects. But the majority of use cases can really benefit from it. For applications/scripts making use of strace and aiming to be compatible across different strace versions it may be too difficult to figure out if `--seccomp-bpf` is supported. It would be very nice to make this decision on strace side.",
