++  "body": "Hi!\r\n\r\nWould it be possible to make this limit\r\nhttps://github.com/strace/strace/blob/dc88a084ebbabde577c3d23982550de998e50ce7/src/unwind-libunwind.c#L134-L135\r\nconfigurable via command-line parameters?\r\n\r\n-----------\r\nContext: i was debugging a complicated chain of processes calling each other, where some of the processes were dying due to a segfault.\r\nI was able to trace the issue down to an endless recursion and inevitable StackOverflow via `strace -f -e 'trace=!all' -k`, however because of the hardcoded depth limit i couldn't find the problematic caller which initiated the recursion, and ended up patching strace for that.",
