++  "body": "When I updated `linux-headers` upto latest `6.5` in `nixpkgs` I noticed that recent `strace` is still `6.4` and it tails to build as https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/pull/252587#issuecomment-1702732344 \r\n\r\n```\r\nio_uring.c: In function 'print_io_sqring_offsets':\r\nio_uring.c:48:16: error: 'const struct io_sqring_offsets' has no member named 'resv2'; did you mean 'resv1'?\r\n   48 |         if (p->resv2) {\r\n      |                ^~~~~\r\n      |                resv1\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe `strace` from `git` builds fine. The fixes are probably in e0da3633669fcb829dd8d902d15443a755bd10fb and others.\r\n\r\nWorth cutting a new `strace` release to trail `linux` release?\r\n\r\nThanks!",
