++  "body": "Within Yocto Project we recently set 5.15 as our minimum kernel version. This changes the way glibc is built such that the accept() call changes to use the accept4 syscall behind the scenes. This causes various test failures in accept, net-yy-inet6, net-yy-inet and\r\nnet-y-unix. I'm not sure how this should be handled in strace?\r\n\r\nAs an example:\r\n\r\ncat  net-yy-inet6.gen.log\r\n--- exp\r\n+++ out\r\n@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@\r\n getsockopt(3<TCPv6:[[::1]:46887]>, SOL_TCP, TCP_MAXSEG, [536], [4]) = 0\r\n socket(AF_INET6, SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_IP) = 4<TCPv6:[17255]>\r\n connect(4<TCPv6:[17255]>, {sa_family=AF_INET6, sin6_port=htons(46887), sin6_flowinfo=htonl(0), inet_pton(AF_INET6, \"::1\", &sin6_addr), sin6_scope_id=0}, 28) = 0\r\n-accept(3<TCPv6:[[::1]:46887]>, {sa_family=AF_INET6, sin6_port=htons(60152), sin6_flowinfo=htonl(0), inet_pton(AF_INET6, \"::1\", &sin6_addr), sin6_scope_id=0}, [28]) = 5<TCPv6:[[::1]:46887->[::1]:60152]>\r\n+accept4(3<TCPv6:[[::1]:46887]>, {sa_family=AF_INET6, sin6_port=htons(60152), sin6_flowinfo=htonl(0), inet_pton(AF_INET6, \"::1\", &sin6_addr), sin6_scope_id=0}, [28], 0) = 5<TCPv6:[[::1]:46887->[::1]:60152]>\r\n getpeername(5<TCPv6:[[::1]:46887->[::1]:60152]>, {sa_family=AF_INET6, sin6_port=htons(60152), sin6_flowinfo=htonl(0), inet_pton(AF_INET6, \"::1\", &sin6_addr), sin6_scope_id=0}, [28]) = 0\r\n getpeername(4<TCPv6:[[::1]:60152->[::1]:46887]>, {sa_family=AF_INET6, sin6_port=htons(46887), sin6_flowinfo=htonl(0), inet_pton(AF_INET6, \"::1\", &sin6_addr), sin6_scope_id=0}, [28]) = 0\r\n setsockopt(4<TCPv6:[[::1]:60152->[::1]:46887]>, SOL_TCP, TCP_MAXSEG, [536], 4) = 0\r\nnet-yy-inet6.gen.test: failed test: ../../src/strace -a22 -yy -eclose,network ../net-yy-inet6 output mismatch\r\nFAIL net-yy-inet6.gen.test (exit status: 1)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
