++  "body": "The Numpy setup install invokes a fairly complex set of child processes when compiling from source.  The install never completes when run within strace.\r\n\r\nThe process tree at the time of the hang looks like this:\r\n```\r\n   372796 pts/5    S      0:00 strace -f -q -s 1024 -e trace=execve python setup.py install\r\n   372799 pts/5    Z      0:00  \\_ [python] <defunct>\r\n   372850 pts/5    D      0:00 /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/collect2 -plugin /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64...\r\n   372851 pts/5    t      0:00  \\_ /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/collect2 -plugin /usr/lib/gcc/x8...\r\n```\r\nThe kernel stacks for the two gcc processes are\r\n(1) for the parent:\r\n```\r\n# cat /proc/372850/stack\r\n[<0>] kernel_clone+0x1fa/0x3d0\r\n[<0>] __do_sys_vfork+0x40/0x60\r\n[<0>] do_syscall_64+0x5c/0xc0\r\n[<0>] entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe+0x61/0xcb\r\n```\r\nand (2) for the hung child:\r\n```\r\n# cat /proc/372851/stack\r\n[<0>] ptrace_stop+0x189/0x360\r\n[<0>] ptrace_do_notify+0x86/0xb0\r\n[<0>] ptrace_notify+0x55/0x80\r\n[<0>] syscall_trace_enter.constprop.0+0xd2/0x1c0\r\n[<0>] syscall_enter_from_user_mode+0x2f/0x40\r\n[<0>] do_syscall_64+0x37/0xc0\r\n[<0>] entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe+0x61/0xcb\r\n```\r\nThe full command lines for these two are:\r\n```\r\n372850 pts/5    D      0:00 /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/collect2 -plugin /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/liblto_plugin.so -plugin-opt=/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/lto-wrapper -plugin-opt=-fresolution=/tmp/ccqZabDV.res -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lgcc -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lgcc_s -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lc -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lgcc -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lgcc_s --build-id --eh-frame-hdr -m elf_x86_64 --hash-style=gnu --as-needed -dynamic-linker /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 -pie -z now -z relro -o _configtest /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/Scrt1.o /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/crti.o /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/crtbeginS.o -L/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11 -L/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu -L/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../../lib -L/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu -L/lib/../lib -L/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu -L/usr/lib/../lib -L/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../.. _configtest.o -lm -lgcc --push-state --as-needed -lgcc_s --pop-state -lc -lgcc --push-state --as-needed -lgcc_s --pop-state /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/crtendS.o /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/crtn.o\r\n```\r\nand\r\n```\r\n372851 pts/5    t      0:00  \\_ /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/collect2 -plugin /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/liblto_plugin.so -plugin-opt=/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/lto-wrapper -plugin-opt=-fresolution=/tmp/ccqZabDV.res -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lgcc -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lgcc_s -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lc -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lgcc -plugin-opt=-pass-through=-lgcc_s --build-id --eh-frame-hdr -m elf_x86_64 --hash-style=gnu --as-needed -dynamic-linker /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 -pie -z now -z relro -o _configtest /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/Scrt1.o /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/crti.o /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/crtbeginS.o -L/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11 -L/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu -L/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../../lib -L/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu -L/lib/../lib -L/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu -L/usr/lib/../lib -L/usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../.. _configtest.o -lm -lgcc --push-state --as-needed -lgcc_s --pop-state -lc -lgcc --push-state --as-needed -lgcc_s --pop-state /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/crtendS.o /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/11/../../../x86_64-linux-gnu/crtn.o\r\n```\r\nTo reproduce:\r\n```\r\ngit clone --branch v1.24.3 https://github.com/numpy/numpy.git\r\nmv numpy numpy-1.24.3\r\ncd numpy-1.24.3\r\ngit submodule update --init\r\nstrace -f -q -s 1024 -e trace=execve python setup.py install\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe following python based strace.py however runs correctly, suggesting that this is not a kernel issue.  My fork of `https://github.com/duanev/python-ptrace` fixes an exit code issue that the current master branch cannot handle (a pull request is pending which links back to the master repo).  After cloning my repo, the command line to use strace.py is:\r\n```\r\n~/git/python-ptrace/strace.py -f -o /tmp/trc.out -e execve -- python setup.py install\r\n```",
