++  "body": "To make 32 bit glibc based platforms prepared for year 2038, all software must be rebuilt with the above flags, which ensure that glibc defines time-sensitive data types with enough bits to go beyond that date.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, this breaks strace's test suite, which would use these data types but continue to directly issue 32 bit versions of system calls. For example, ppoll (first lines are printed by strace, second lines by tests/ppoll - they should match but they aren't):\r\n\r\n```\r\n# strace -s 2 -e ppoll tests/ppoll\r\nppoll(NULL, 4207869677, NULL, NULL, 3134983661) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll(NULL, 4207869677, NULL, NULL, 3134983661) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll(0xb7d70000, 42, 0xb7d70008, 0xb7d70010, 8) = -1 EFAULT (Bad address)\r\nppoll(0xb7d70000, 42, 0xb7d70008, 0xb7d70010, 8) = -1 EFAULT (Bad address)\r\nppoll(NULL, 0, {tv_sec=-559038737, tv_nsec=0}, NULL, 8) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll(NULL, 0, {tv_sec=3735928559, tv_nsec=4207869677}, NULL, 8) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll(NULL, 0, {tv_sec=-559038737, tv_nsec=3405705229}, NULL, 8) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll(NULL, 0, {tv_sec=-3819351491602432273, tv_nsec=4207869677}, NULL, 8) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll([{fd=3, events=POLLIN|POLLPRI|POLLRDNORM|POLLRDBAND}, {fd=4, events=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM|POLLWRBAND}, ...], 4, {tv_sec=42, tv_nsec=0}, [USR2 CHLD], 8) = 2 ([{fd=4, revents=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM}, {fd=6, revent)\r\nppoll([{fd=3, events=POLLIN|POLLPRI|POLLRDNORM|POLLRDBAND}, {fd=4, events=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM|POLLWRBAND}, ...], 4, {tv_sec=42, tv_nsec=999999999}, [USR2 CHLD], 8) = 2 ([{fd=4, revents=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM}, {fd=6)\r\nppoll([{fd=4, events=POLLIN|POLLPRI|POLLRDNORM|POLLRDBAND}, {fd=3, events=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM|POLLWRBAND}], 2, {tv_sec=0, tv_nsec=0}, ~[HUP KILL STOP], 8) = 0 (Timeout)\r\nppoll([{fd=4, events=POLLIN|POLLPRI|POLLRDNORM|POLLRDBAND}, {fd=3, events=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM|POLLWRBAND}], 2, {tv_sec=0, tv_nsec=999}, ~[HUP KILL STOP], 8) = 0 (Timeout)\r\n+++ exited with 0 +++\r\n+++ exited with 0 +++\r\n```\r\n\r\nI quickly hacked that particular test to use the 64bit syscall to see what happens:\r\n```\r\ndiff --git a/tests/ppoll.c b/tests/ppoll.c\r\nindex 71f9ec2..d37e807 100644\r\n--- a/tests/ppoll.c\r\n+++ b/tests/ppoll.c\r\n@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ sys_ppoll(const kernel_ulong_t ufds,\r\n          const kernel_ulong_t sigmask,\r\n          const kernel_ulong_t sigsetsize)\r\n {\r\n-       long rc = syscall(__NR_ppoll, ufds, nfds, tsp, sigmask, sigsetsize);\r\n+       long rc = syscall(__NR_ppoll_time64, ufds, nfds, tsp, sigmask, sigsetsize);\r\n        errstr = sprintrc(rc);\r\n        return rc;\r\n }\r\n```\r\n\r\nThings improve (tv_sec at least matches), but aren't completely resolved:\r\n```\r\n# strace -s 2 -e ppoll_time64 tests/ppoll\r\nppoll_time64(NULL, 4207869677, NULL, NULL, 3134983661) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll(NULL, 4207869677, NULL, NULL, 3134983661) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll_time64(0xb7d47000, 42, 0xb7d47008, 0xb7d47010, 8) = -1 EFAULT (Bad address)\r\nppoll(0xb7d47000, 42, 0xb7d47008, 0xb7d47010, 8) = -1 EFAULT (Bad address)\r\nppoll_time64(NULL, 0, {tv_sec=3735928559, tv_nsec=18446744073622453997}, NULL, 8) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll(NULL, 0, {tv_sec=3735928559, tv_nsec=4207869677}, NULL, 8) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll_time64(NULL, 0, {tv_sec=-3819351491602432273, tv_nsec=18446744073622453997}, NULL, 8) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll(NULL, 0, {tv_sec=-3819351491602432273, tv_nsec=4207869677}, NULL, 8) = -1 EINVAL (Invalid argument)\r\nppoll_time64([{fd=3, events=POLLIN|POLLPRI|POLLRDNORM|POLLRDBAND}, {fd=4, events=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM|POLLWRBAND}, ...], 4, {tv_sec=42, tv_nsec=18446744070414584319}, [USR2 CHLD], 8) = 2 ([{fd=4, revents=POLLOUT|)\r\nppoll([{fd=3, events=POLLIN|POLLPRI|POLLRDNORM|POLLRDBAND}, {fd=4, events=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM|POLLWRBAND}, ...], 4, {tv_sec=42, tv_nsec=999999999}, [USR2 CHLD], 8) = 2 ([{fd=4, revents=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM}, {fd=6)\r\nppoll_time64([{fd=4, events=POLLIN|POLLPRI|POLLRDNORM|POLLRDBAND}, {fd=3, events=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM|POLLWRBAND}], 2, {tv_sec=0, tv_nsec=999}, ~[HUP KILL STOP], 8) = 0 (Timeout)\r\nppoll([{fd=4, events=POLLIN|POLLPRI|POLLRDNORM|POLLRDBAND}, {fd=3, events=POLLOUT|POLLWRNORM|POLLWRBAND}], 2, {tv_sec=0, tv_nsec=999}, ~[HUP KILL STOP], 8) = 0 (Timeout)\r\n+++ exited with 0 +++\r\n+++ exited with 0 +++\r\n```",
