++  "body": "kfd (/dev/kfd) is an interface exposed by amdgpu kernel driver for user space drivers (e.g. ROCm)\r\n \r\n### FIXME \r\n\r\nKD and KFD both use the 'K' base. Fortunately they currently do not overlap and can be distinguished from NR. However, as KFD is gradually adding ioctls, one day they may overlap.\r\n\r\nMore generously, how do we decode ioctls arg with the same base? We already have `ioctl_next_match` for displaying ioctls with the same code, do we have similar mechanisms?\r\n\r\n### Note\r\n\r\nTODOs in code will not be addressed in this patchset. They could be implemented later when I get the time.\r\n\r\nAlso, the variable length array handling for `struct kfd_ioctl_svm_attribute attrs[];` could be generalized to e.g. `defs.h` then `print_field.h`. I think `tfetch_obj` after the end of the struct is quite unsafe. If kernel returned an invalid `nattr`, e.g. -1, then we will access the whole memory. What's your opinion on this.\r\n\r\n### TODO\r\n\r\n* The FIXME mentioned above\r\n* Tests\r\n",
