++  "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\nI tried to upload 6.1 to Debian (experimental) as got test failures on mips64el and mipsel architectures.\r\n\r\nThe full build logs are available at:\r\n* https://buildd.debian.org/status/fetch.php?pkg=strace&arch=mips64el&ver=6.1-0.1%7Eexp2&stamp=1674843235&raw=0\r\n* https://buildd.debian.org/status/fetch.php?pkg=strace&arch=mipsel&ver=6.1-0.1%7Eexp2&stamp=1674844648&raw=0\r\n\r\nI tried to analyze the logs and as far as I can tell the failures boils down to:\r\n\r\n# mips64el\r\n\r\nptrace_syscall_info seem to be the root cause for all test failures!\r\n\r\n```\r\n../../tests/ptrace_syscall_info.c:246: ../../tests/ptrace_syscall_info.c:246: #1: entry stop mismatch\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n# mipsel\r\n\r\n\r\nMost test-case failures are caused by (or a variant of this test segfaulting):\r\n```\r\n+ ../sockopt-sol_socket\r\nSegmentation fault\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut there are also multiple tests that fails for various reasons (diff between expected and output).\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n(There are also failures on other non-release architectures that can currently be seen at: https://buildd.debian.org/status/package.php?p=strace&suite=experimental  ... click the status column for respective architecture for full build log.)\r\n",
