++  "body": "Trying to compile strace with lib-unwind so that I can use the -k option to print stack trace. Following were the steps\r\n\r\n> sudo yum install -y autoconf automake libunwind libunwind-devel gcc\r\n> cd /var/tmp\r\n> git clone https://github.com/strace/strace.git\r\n> cd strace\r\n> ./bootstrap\r\n> ./configure --with-libunwind\r\n\r\nThe ./configure --with-libunwind failed with the following error\r\n\r\n> checking libunwind-ptrace.h usability... no\r\n> checking libunwind-ptrace.h presence... no\r\n> checking for libunwind-ptrace.h... no\r\n> configure: error: in `/var/tmp/strace':\r\n> configure: error: failed to find libunwind-ptrace.h\r\n\r\nI see this issue [reported here](https://github.com/strace/strace/issues/165#issuecomment-739245518) which was closed without addressing why strace wouldn't compile with --with-libunwind option. Trying to use strace -k for which it has to be run with the --with-libunwind option.\r\n\r\n",
