++  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nFirst of all, thank you for making and maintaining this very useful tool. \r\n\r\nI'm trying to get a list of open files from the Apache webserver with strace version 6.0 in an Alpine container:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/ # strace -V\r\nstrace -- version 6.0\r\nCopyright (c) 1991-2022 The strace developers <https://strace.io>.\r\nThis is free software; see the source for copying conditions.  There is NO\r\nwarranty; not even for MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.\r\n\r\nOptional features enabled: stack-trace=libdw stack-demangle no-m32-mpers no-mx32-mpers\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm trying the command \r\n\r\n``strace -f -z -e trace=open httpd -D FOREGROUND``\r\n\r\nFor files that are opened in the main process this works fine: it shows the filename, for example:\r\n\r\n``open(\"/lib/libuuid.so.1\", O_RDONLY|O_LARGEFILE|O_CLOEXEC) = 3``\r\n\r\nFor files in the sub processes, I'm getting hexadecimal values:\r\n\r\n``[pid    38] open(0x7ffce6b3a200, O_RDONLY|O_LARGEFILE) = 11``\r\n\r\nIs there a flag to get the \"real\" filenames? Is there another way for me outside strace to know the real file name based on the hexadecimal value? Is this normal behaviour, something that cannot be fixed or is it a bug?\r\n\r\nThank you for your help,\r\n\r\nFrederique",
