++  "body": "Hi, 5.18 builds but 5.19 fails to compile on alpha, kernel+headers 5.19.\r\n\r\n```\r\nalpha-unknown-linux-gnu-gcc -DHAVE_CONFIG_H   -I./linux/alpha -I./linux/alpha -I./linux/generic -I./linux/generic -I. -I. -I../bundled/linux/arch/alpha/include/uapi -I../bundled/linux/include/uapi -DIN_STRACE=1      -I./bundled/linux/arch/alpha/include/uapi -I./bundled/linux/include/uapi -Wall -Wextra -Wno-missing-field-initializers -Wno-unused-parameter -Wdate-time -Wformat-security -Wimplicit-fallthrough=5 -Winit-self -Wlogical-op -Wmissing-prototypes -Wnested-externs -Wold-style-definition -Wtrampolines -Wundef -Wwrite-strings  -mieee -O2 -pipe -mcpu=ev4 -c -o libstrace_a-printsiginfo.o `test -f 'printsiginfo.c' || echo './'`printsiginfo.c\r\nIn file included from printsiginfo.c:16:\r\nprintsiginfo.c: In function \u2018print_si_info\u2019:\r\nprintsiginfo.c:191:50: error: \u2018siginfo_t\u2019 has no member named \u2018si_trapno\u2019; did you mean \u2018si_errno\u2019?\r\n  191 |                         PRINT_FIELD_XVAL_D(*sip, si_trapno, alpha_trap_codes,\r\n      |                                                  ^~~~~~~~~\r\ndefs.h:1854:17: note: in definition of macro \u2018sign_extend_unsigned_to_ll\u2019\r\n 1854 |         (sizeof(v) == sizeof(char) ? (long long) (char) (v) : \\\r\n      |                 ^\r\n```\r\n\r\n(lots of repeats in the same file, just including the meaningful error here)\r\n\r\nPresumably caused by https://github.com/strace/strace/commit/9fd4989f7d14f4213627d521626fbecdd52838eb?\r\n\r\nMaybe this kernel change is related?  https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/87h7gvxx7l.fsf_-_@disp2133/",
