++  "body": "Hello, here is a bug fix for umovestr :\r\n\r\n```\r\n--- a/src/ucopy.c\r\n+++ b/src/ucopy.c\r\n@@ -432,7 +432,7 @@ umovestr(struct tcb *const tcp, kernel_ulong_t addr, unsigned int len,\r\n \t\t\tchar *nul_addr = memchr(laddr, '\\0', r);\r\n \r\n \t\t\tif (nul_addr)\r\n-\t\t\t\treturn (nul_addr - laddr) + 1;\r\n+\t\t\t\treturn (nul_addr - laddr) + 1 + nread;\r\n \t\t\taddr += r;\r\n \t\t\tladdr += r;\r\n \t\t\tnread += r;\r\n```\r\nwhen it takes more than 1 iteration calling vm_read_mem, then umovestr\r\nreturns an incorrect number of bytes.  This should fix it.\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\n-Truxton",
