++  "body": "The [src/Makefile.am](https://github.com/strace/strace/blob/a0f7df7d3783074b5aac66ea4e55646524164e70/src/Makefile.am) and some build shell scripts use `sed -r` which isn't POSIX standard.  Newer versions of GNU sed recommend using `-E` instead: https://www.gnu.org/software/sed/manual/sed.html#Command_002dLine-Options\r\n\r\n> Historically this was a GNU extension, but the -E extension has since been added to the POSIX standard (http://austingroupbugs.net/view.php?id=528), so use -E for portability. GNU sed has accepted -E as an undocumented option for years, and *BSD seds have accepted -E for years as well, but scripts that use -E might not port to other older systems.\r\n\r\n`sed -r` also appears in a number test-related scripts, but their appearance there don't interfere with the build process.",
