++  "body": "How can I use strace to trace a program that already forked a few children and it is already executing before running strace -p on it?\r\n\r\nMy test program:\r\n\r\n```\r\n#include <stdio.h>\r\n#include <unistd.h>\r\n#include <sys/types.h>\r\n#include <sys/stat.h>\r\n#include <fcntl.h>\r\n\r\nint main(int argc, char *argv[])\r\n{\r\n  int f1, f2, f3;\r\n  f1 = open(\"/dev/null\", O_RDWR);\r\n  f2 = open(\"/dev/null\", O_RDWR);\r\n  f3 = open(\"/dev/null\", O_RDWR);\r\n\r\nfork();\r\nfork();\r\n\r\n  int ck;\r\n  do {\r\n    ck = 0;\r\n    ck += lseek(f1, 0, SEEK_CUR);\r\n    ck += lseek(f2, 0, SEEK_CUR);\r\n    ck += lseek(f3, 0, SEEK_CUR);\r\n    printf(\"I'm aliveee...\\n\");\r\n    sleep(15);\r\n  } while (ck != -3);\r\n\r\n  return 0;\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf I use strace -f -p (pid of the running program) I only get what the main thread does...\r\nI guess I should use multiple -p options to trace them all but I also think there should/could be a command line switch to automatically do so.\r\n",
