++  "body": "On strace 5.10 (archlinux packaging) when tracing a process that forks you can see parent syscalls in the child process trace file (and these syscalls will be missing from the parent trace file). Process launched with `strace -ff --output=strace.txt ./exe`\r\n\r\nIn my case the child process can be seen getting two different results from getpid().\r\n\r\n```\r\ngetpid()                                = 616723\r\ngettid()                                = 616724\r\n```\r\n\r\nAdditional calls including those return fd's were also misattributed to the child process. On my machine this happens consistently and these calls are always misattributed after 10 or so tests. Let me know if there is any other information I might be be able to provide.\r\n\r\n--- edit\r\nAnd because this is not mentioned in the man page I assume it is a bug, if its known that this can happen a mention in the man page would be helpful.",
