++  "body": "Currently it is possible only to not attach to child processes at all or to follow forks infinitely. Sometimes something like `strace -f1 ...` could be useful if a process is launched by some other launcher (like systemd), but you are not interested in tracing of all its descendants, except of the main process. So the option that would allow to limit followed process tree depth could be useful.\r\nReal use case: I need to debug how the system session \"systemd\" is starting the user session \"systemd\". But I don't want to log of how the user session \"systemd\" starts all of the user services.",
