++  "body": "I'm building on an old system, where sg_io_v4.c (and tests/ioctl_sg_io_v4.c) fails with\r\n```\r\n/usr/include/linux/bsg.h:11: error: expected specifier-qualifier-list before \u2018__s32\u2019\r\n```\r\nand therefore `struct sg_io_v4` isn't resolved. It turns out that `__s32` is defined in `<linux/types.h>`. If I include that right before `<linux/bsg.h>`, strace builds fine.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure whether you would change this in configure.ac (as in 3857665065f09f750bfcdd150930e663291b6616) or in the respective source files (as in commit 7bbf7813f9304d935e1f96b259b834789ad457ef). Therefore no pull request from me. ;) ",
