++  "body": "Hi all,\r\n\r\nI have recently discover the following behavior : if a binary does not have the read permision, strace is not able to retrieve some information.\r\n\r\nFor example, take the following program:\r\n```C\r\n#include<stdio.h>\r\n\r\nint main() {\r\n    printf(\"hello world!\\n\");\r\n    return 0;\r\n}\r\n```\r\nwhen the binary has the read permission, strace outputs:\r\n\r\n> write(1, \"hello world!\\n\", 13hello world!\r\n)          = 13\r\n\r\nbut if this permission is removed, it outputs:\r\n> write(1, 0x563967a612a0, 13hello world!\r\n)            = 13\r\n\r\nPlease note the difference betweenthe second parameters of each call.\r\n\r\nIt is a bug? An inherent limitation of ptrace? Something else altogether?\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks in advance. ",
