++  "body": "Good afternoon, I'm trying to compile strace for Android aarch64 \r\n\r\n```\r\nexport CC = / usr / bin / aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc\r\nexport CFLAGS = \"- O2 -static\"\r\nexport LDFLAGS = \"- static -pthread\"\r\n\r\ngit clone https://github.com/strace/strace.git\r\ncd strace\r\nautoconf\r\n./bootstrap\r\n\r\n./configure --host = aarch64-linux --enable-mpers = no\r\n\r\nmake\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd an error comes out: \r\n\r\n```\r\ngcc -DHAVE_CONFIG_H   -I./linux/aarch64 -I./linux/aarch64 -I./linux -I./linux -I. -I.      -Wall -Wempty-body -Wformat-security -Wignored-qualifiers -Wimplicit-fallthrough=5 -Winit-self -Wlogical-op -Wmissing-parameter-type -Wnested-externs -Wold-style-declaration -Wold-style-definition -Woverride-init -Wsign-compare -Wtype-limits -Wwrite-strings -Werror   -g -O2 -MT libstrace_a-syscall.o -MD -MP -MF .deps/libstrace_a-syscall.Tpo -c -o libstrace_a-syscall.o test -f 'syscall.c' || echo './'syscall.c\r\nIn file included from syscall.c:1025:\r\n./linux/aarch64/arch_regs.c:31:22: error: field \u2018aarch64_r\u2019 has incomplete type\r\n   31 |  struct user_pt_regs aarch64_r;\r\n      |                      ^~~~~\r\nmake[2]: * [Makefile:7182: libstrace_a-syscall.o] \u041e\u0448\u0438\u0431\u043a\u0430 1\r\n```",
