++  "body": "This [Stack Overflow question](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/63464497/what-is-the-size-of-proc-u-fd-u/63464598?noredirect=1#comment112224687_63464598) lead to an observation by [bruno](https://stackoverflow.com/users/2458991/bruno) that the [following code](https://github.com/strace/strace/blob/master/util.c#L487) is incorrect:\r\n\r\n```c\r\nchar path[sizeof(\"/proc/%u/fd/%u\") + 2 * sizeof(int)*3];\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhere `sizeof(\"...\")` obviously returns the same size for everything, that being of a `char*` pointer.\r\n\r\nThis should be:\r\n\r\n```c\r\nchar path[strlen(\"/proc/%u/fd/%u\") + 2 * sizeof(int)*3];\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe difference here is enough you could force a buffer overflow with unexpectedly large values for PID and FD.\r\n\r\nAnother thing to note is that string is also duplicated, used later in the code, and could be assigned to a variable that's used in both places. There's a potential for a mistake here when one is changed but the other is not.",
