++  "body": "`strace` prints both forms of the socket syscalls - the legacy ones multiplexed on `SYS_socketcall`, and the modern individual syscalls - identically, and does not seem to offer any option to distinguish them. This makes it really difficult to debug issues caused by which version a binary is using, e.g. incompatibility with an older kernel that lacks the new syscalls, or behavior of fallback if the caller supports both.\r\n\r\nA nice general solution might be adding an option to print the syscall number for all syscalls. I'm not sure if an option specific to `socketcall` makes sense, but at this point it might make sense to just *always* print the old ones as `socketcall(...` and the new ones with their names. I'm not attached to any particular solution, but I think something should be done to resolve the ambiguity and make it possible to debug these syscalls.\r\n",
