++  "body": "#138 fixed the build for the new kernel, but headers from older kernels now cause build failures here:\r\n```\r\n[   57s] In file included from ./static_assert.h:11,\r\n[   57s]                  from types/check-io_uring.c:3:\r\n[   57s] types/check-io_uring.c:21:1: error: static assertion failed: \"struct io_cqring_offsets size mismatch, please update the decoder or fix the kernel\"\r\n[   57s]    21 | static_assert(sizeof(struct io_cqring_offsets) <= offsetof(struct_io_cqring_offsets, resv2),\r\n[   57s]       | ^~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n```\r\n`offsetof` `resv2` is definitely smaller than `sizeof` the whole structure. So I think the assert is incorrect. Perhaps it should be using `offsetofend`:\r\n```\r\nstatic_assert(sizeof(struct io_cqring_offsets) <= offsetofend(struct_io_cqring_offsets, resv2),\r\n```",
