++  "body": "When tracing batch jobs (like `make(1)`) it's immesurably useful to get also user/kernel CPU time for each process/thread beside overall clock time for whole process (which we can obtain as difference between `execve` and `+++ exit code` times.\r\n\r\nNote: hooking `wait` in parent process is useless, because it won't help with detached threads and daemonized children. And often used `wait4(..., NULL)` won't pass `rusage` back anyway.\r\n\r\nExpectations are to print plain list of values in `struct rusage` order:\r\n```strace\r\n180535 1582654045.919886 +++ exited with 0 +++ [4.232111, 0.0, ...]\r\n```\r\nHow hard is it to implement?",
