++  "body": "Literally what I propose is one of:\r\n1. New one-argument syntax which allows modifiers in any position: \r\n```bash\r\nstrace -e trace=%process,%file,!clone,!wait4,!read,!write\r\n```\r\nIn this case it would also be good to have regex (and extend it by inverting) in any position\r\n```bash\r\nstrace -e trace=%process,%file,!clone,!wait4,!/^read.*/,!/^write.*/\r\n```\r\n\r\n2. OR:(better? simpler?):  **keep existing syntax** and use global FSM to incrementally modify mask by each next cmdline argument\r\n```bash\r\nstrace -e trace=%process,%file -e trace=!clone,wait4 -e trace=!/^(read|write).*/\r\n```",
