++  "body": "I use strace to analyze current forking inefficiencies of legacy build system:\r\n```bash\r\nstrace --seccomp-bpf -qftttvzs4096 -e verbose='execve,execveat' -X raw -e trace='%process' -e signal=none -- make\r\n```\r\nLiterally, for analysis what I need to extract is these three things:\r\n* timestamps of create/exit of each child process recursively (execve/execveat/exit)\r\n* whole unabbreviated ARGV of each process (but I don't need ENVP)\r\n* process tree -- which PID had spawned which other ones (clone/vfork)\r\n\r\nThe problem is: our build system environment is awfully big, but I can only filter `-e verbose=...` output  per-syscall, and not with per-position precision. Extrapolating my half-hour experiment, total build will result in insanely huge log files ~1TB.\r\nAt least I haven't found any way to do this nor in documentation, nor source code.\r\n\r\n1. Have I missed some related info in maillist on any ongoing enhancements?\r\n2. Is anybody interested in implementing generic per-argument `verbose` filtering?\r\n3. Will dirty changes only to `x86_64/execve` and additional flag `--hide-environment` be acceptable contribution?\r\n4. Maybe `strace` isn't the best tool for described above purpose. Do you have any suggestions?",
