++  "body": "I was just wondering why when I download strace off of sourceforge I already get the ./configure. Where as if I try to build from the source here, my instinct is to run aclocal, but it turns out that is not correct. My next instinct is to read `README-configure` which is also not correct.... then I realize based off a different issue the source of truth is in `INSTALL-git.md` which leads me to `./bootstrap`.\r\n\r\nSo I am assuming that you all also own the sourceforge. So why not also keep the configure in the repo here, or eliminate the need for the `sed`s, also wondering the \"why\" for that. And why sourceforge not github seems to be the best place to get the source for strace from.\r\n\r\nAnyways, thanks for the transparency here, would really love to know why :)",
