++  "body": "I understand I\u2019m filing this issue quite late, but Debian shipped strace 4.21 for a long time, so I didn\u2019t notice this until recently. Also, apologies in advance for pulling a https://xkcd.com/1172/\r\n\r\nFor working on the nftables package in Go (https://github.com/google/nftables), I was using strace to quickly get a hex byte sequence to plug into my unit tests to verify that my package generates netlink messages which are byte-for-byte equal with what `nft(8)` produces. See e.g. https://github.com/google/nftables/blob/900c47abbbaf6e391146125870c0f16d3c124330/nftables_test.go#L114-L140\r\n\r\nThis worked fine in strace 4.21, but newer versions changed their output (due to commit https://github.com/strace/strace/commit/073d93827f77e8787cdb7ec1ae28b60866334482 and possibly others) to actually decode netlink messages instead of just displaying the raw bytes.\r\n\r\nSo, instead of the following (not using code blocks so that we get line wrapping):\r\n\r\n`# strace-4.21/strace -f -v -x -s 2048 -etrace=sendmsg nft add chain ip6 filter forward '{' type filter hook forward priority 0 \\; '}'`\r\nsendmsg(3, {msg_name={sa_family=AF_NETLINK, nl_pid=0, nl_groups=00000000}, msg_namelen=12, msg_iov=[{iov_base=[{{len=20, type=NFNL_MSG_BATCH_BEGIN, flags=NLM_F_REQUEST, seq=0, pid=0}, \"\\x00\\x00\\x0a\\x00\"}, {{len=76, type=NFNL_SUBSYS_NFTABLES<<8|NFT_MSG_NEWCHAIN, flags=NLM_F_REQUEST|NLM_F_CREATE, seq=1, pid=0}, \"\\x0a\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x0b\\x00\\x01\\x00\\x66\\x69\\x6c\\x74\\x65\\x72\\x00\\x00\\x0c\\x00\\x03\\x00\\x66\\x6f\\x72\\x77\\x61\\x72\\x64\\x00\\x14\\x00\\x04\\x80\\x08\\x00\\x01\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x02\\x08\\x00\\x02\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x0b\\x00\\x07\\x00\\x66\\x69\\x6c\\x74\\x65\\x72\\x00\\x00\"}, {{len=20, type=NFNL_MSG_BATCH_END, flags=NLM_F_REQUEST, seq=2, pid=0}, \"\\x00\\x00\\x0a\\x00\"}], iov_len=116}], msg_iovlen=1, msg_controllen=0, msg_flags=0}, 0) = 116\r\n+++ exited with 0 +++\r\n\r\n\u2026I now see:\r\n\r\n`# strace -f -v -x -s 2048 -etrace=sendmsg nft add chain ip6 filter forward '{' type filter hook forward priority 0 \\; '}'`\r\nsendmsg(3, {msg_name={sa_family=AF_NETLINK, nl_pid=0, nl_groups=00000000}, msg_namelen=12, msg_iov=[{iov_base=[{{len=20, type=NFNL_MSG_BATCH_BEGIN, flags=NLM_F_REQUEST, seq=0, pid=0}, {nfgen_family=AF_UNSPEC, version=NFNETLINK_V0, res_id=htons(2560)}, {{len=76, type=NFNL_SUBSYS_NFTABLES<<8|NFT_MSG_NEWCHAIN, flags=NLM_F_REQUEST|NLM_F_CREATE, seq=1, pid=0}, {nfgen_family=AF_INET6, version=NFNETLINK_V0, res_id=htons(0), [{{nla_len=11, nla_type=NFNETLINK_V1}, \"\\x66\\x69\\x6c\\x74\\x65\\x72\\x00\"}, {{nla_len=12, nla_type=0x3}, \"\\x66\\x6f\\x72\\x77\\x61\\x72\\x64\\x00\"}, {{nla_len=20, nla_type=NLA_F_NESTED|0x4}, \"\\x08\\x00\\x01\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x02\\x08\\x00\\x02\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\\x00\"}, {{nla_len=11, nla_type=0x7}, \"\\x66\\x69\\x6c\\x74\\x65\\x72\\x00\"}]}, {{len=20, type=NFNL_MSG_BATCH_END, flags=NLM_F_REQUEST, seq=2, pid=0}, {nfgen_family=AF_UNSPEC, version=NFNETLINK_V0, res_id=htons(2560)}], iov_len=116}], msg_iovlen=1, msg_controllen=0, msg_flags=0}, 0) = 116\r\n+++ exited with 0 +++\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is fine per se, of course, but note that I am running strace with the `-x` flag. Specifying `-X raw` also has no effect.\r\n\r\nAm I missing something? Is there a way to obtain the old output that I just can\u2019t find?\r\n\r\nIf no, could such a way be added? Maybe the nft decoder should honor `-X raw`?\r\n\r\nThanks in advance,\r\n\r\nPS: As a temporary workaround, one can recompile strace with the following patch applied:\r\n```diff\r\n--- i/netlink_netfilter.c\r\n+++ w/netlink_netfilter.c\r\n@@ -33,6 +33,9 @@ decode_netlink_netfilter(struct tcb *const tcp,\r\n \r\n        struct nfgenmsg nfmsg;\r\n \r\n+printstr_ex(tcp, addr, len, QUOTE_FORCE_HEX);\r\n+return true;\r\n+\r\n        if (len < sizeof(nfmsg))\r\n                printstr_ex(tcp, addr, len, QUOTE_FORCE_HEX);\r\n        else if (!umove_or_printaddr(tcp, addr, &nfmsg)) {\r\n```",
