++  "body": "Dear Sir,Madam,\r\nMy name is Hoang Dang Kien.I'm a researcher in VietNam National University\r\nI run strace on an ELF file in MIPS architecture ,O32 OS and received a result . This is a piece of result.\r\n\r\nread(21, \"7\", 1)                        = 1\r\nread(21, \"u\", 1)                        = 1\r\nread(21, \"4\", 1)                        = 1\r\nread(21, \"\\r\", 1)                       = 1\r\nread(21, \"\\n\", 1)                       = 1\r\nsvr4_symlink()                          = 4288\r\nsvr4_munmap()                           = -1 (errno 4249)\r\nsvr4_exit()                             = -1 (errno 4249)\r\nsvr4_exit()                             = 4003\r\ngetpriority(0x75 /* PRIO_??? */, 144769024) = -1 (errno 4173)\r\nsvr4_syscall()                          = -1 (errno 4263)\r\nsvr4_syscall()                          = 4263\r\n\r\nI looked inside the file /usr/include/mips-linux-gnu/asm/unistd.h. I can see Syscalls as read,exit,syscall, getpriority but I can't see any Syscalls start with svr4. I know that, svr4 Syscalls start at 0 and my OS (O32) Syscall start at 4000. So please explain me , Is svr4_exit is a Syscall or not? And where can I find the systemcall list used by strace? Thank you so much.",
