++  "body": "One of my projects uses strace extensively generating logs of up to 100GB In order to perform quite time intensive analysis. We would benefit tremendously if we could make a modified version of strace that performs some preprocessing and write to an database.\r\n\r\nIdeally we would use strace as an [library](https://github.com/strace/strace/issues/70) but I don't understand strace well enough to perform this modifications yet.\r\n\r\nSo I'm wondering, could someone point me in the relevant source locations to patch strace so it can write to eg. a custom destination(eg. a database)?\r\n\r\nIf you think there is any value to add an option to strace to load a user-supplied callback from a shared-library I'd be happy to make a PR once I manage with your help to make the appropriate modifications\r\n",
