++  "body": "Hey everyone.  As part of another project I needed to enhance the [rr](https://github.com/mozilla/rr) debugger to output system call information in strace's format as the application under debug was executing.  I hacked together something that got the job done by compiling strace into a static library and directly calling the entry and exit decode/trace/finish functions after setting the required state.  I had to to supply a my own umoven() and umovestr() as well.  Is this a feature for which there might be an audience if it could be put together in a clean enough fashion?  I likely won't have the time to do the required reorganization to make things publishable but I would be glad to help out if someone thinks this is interesting enough to take on.  \r\n\r\nEither way, the project has my appreciation for maintaining a codebase that is easy to understand and work with.\r\n",
