++  "body": "I was wondering if there's an appropriate limit for \"sane\" UID/GID values and after some pondering decided to limit this to what `/etc/login.defs` specifies:\r\n\r\n```\r\n# Min/max values for automatic uid selection in useradd\r\n#\r\nUID_MAX\t\t\t60000\r\nGID_MAX\t\t\t60000\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe intent was to not use anything in the sub-uid/gid range by accident.\r\n\r\nWith the assumption that it is easier to be loosen a limit rather than to tighten it, I wanted to be conservative here.\r\n\r\nThis can be dropped if you think that strace should not be policing this value.",
