++  "body": "I agree that it wouldn't make sense for an ioctl to be defined with _IOC_NONE with a non-zero _IOC_SIZE.  However, I figured, in the off chance that there are some ioctls like this, that the most helpful thing that strace could do for the user (in the absence of any knowledge of which direction the data was flowing) was to try to print the buffer both before and after.\r\n\r\nIf not this, what behavior do you think would be better?",
