++  "body": "When we need to check whether the syscall returned an error, we use `syserror(tcp)`.\r\nThat is, if `tcp->u_rval >= 0` is a syscall error check, it should rather be `!syserror(tcp)`.\r\n\r\nIf we want to check whether some `kernel_long_t val` is a positive int, then we would have to check\r\n`val == (int) val && (int) val > 0`.",
