++  "body": "Test covers `CLOCK_AUX + 7` (last valid) but not `CLOCK_AUX_LAST + 1` (first invalid):\nan off-by-one error where upper bound is `'<= CLOCK_AUX + 8'` instead of `'<= CLOCK_AUX_LAST'` would pass tests; value 24 would incorrectly print as `'CLOCK_AUX + 8'` instead of `'CLOCK_???'`.\n\nNo test coverage for -Xverbose, -Xraw, or -Xabbrev modes with CLOCK_AUX values:\nmissing VERBOSE comment wrapper goes undetected; with `-Xverbose`, output is `'16 CLOCK_AUX + 0'` instead of `'16 /* CLOCK_AUX + 0 */'`, causing user confusion or test mismatch if xlat modes are tested.",
