++  "body": "Okay, I'm starting to remember now, the macros were added to `include/linux/posix-timers.h` in `v2.6.39-rc1~508^2~11` \"posix clocks: Introduce dynamic clocks\", but that header has never been exposed as UAPI, as kernel developers do not tend to have a lot of care about exposing definitions for the user space, and an attempt to get it there[1] has failed.  Ultimately. the macros themselves have been removed from the kernel source in `v4.16-rc1~176^2~54` \"posix-timers: Prevent UB from shifting negative signed value\". So, yeah, it seems that the only way is to just bundle clockid-related definitions.\r\n\r\n[1] https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20190923130531.GA27774@asgard.redhat.com/",
